":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","content":"Every EasyWebinar webinar has an **Analytics** tab that shows how many people reached each stage of that webinar and where the rest dropped away. It has three views: **Overview** for the funnel, engagement and offer numbers, **People** for the individuals behind those numbers, and **Revenue** for what the webinar earned. A date range at the top limits everything on the page to the period you choose."},"1487":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-44","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#at-a-glance","content":"|                      |                                    |\n| -------------------- | ---------------------------------- |\n| **Where to find it** | Open a webinar → **Analytics** tab |","table":"table-0"},"1488":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-45","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#at-a-glance","content":"|           |                                          |\n| --------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| **Views** | **Overview**, **People** and **Revenue** |","table":"table-0"},"1489":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-46","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#at-a-glance","content":"|                 |                                                              |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Time period** | A date range with **Apply**, covering everything on the page |","table":"table-0"},"1490":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-47","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#at-a-glance","content":"|                    |                                                                                                     |\n| ------------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Funnel metrics** | **Visitors**, **Registered**, **Live Attended**, **Replay Watched**, **Total Attended**, **Missed** |","table":"table-0"},"1491":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-48","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#at-a-glance","content":"|                   |                                                                                            |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| **Offer metrics** | **Offers Performance**, **Views to Clicks**, **Clicks to Purchases**, **Revenue by Offer** |","table":"table-0"},"1492":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-49","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#at-a-glance","content":"|                        |                                                     |\n| ---------------------- | --------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Engagement metrics** | **Chat** message totals and **Questions & Answers** |","table":"table-0"},"1493":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-50","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#at-a-glance","content":"|                       |                              |\n| --------------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| **Audience location** | **Registrations by country** |","table":"table-0"},"1494":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-51","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#at-a-glance","content":"|             |                                                                                         |\n| ----------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Revenue** | **Total Revenue**, **Paid Registrations**, **Revenue by Source**, and every transaction |","table":"table-0"},"1495":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-52","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#at-a-glance","content":"|                   |                              |\n| ----------------- | ---------------------------- |\n| **Webinar types** | Live, simulive and evergreen |","table":"table-0"},"1496":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-53","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#what-it-is","content":"The Analytics tab is the per-webinar report. It answers two questions: how many people got through each stage, from landing on the registration page to watching, and where the others stopped."},"1497":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-54","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#what-it-is","content":"The **Overview** view is built around a funnel. People arrive at the registration page, some register, some of those attend live or watch the replay, and some never show up. Below the funnel sit the numbers for what happened during the session: chat, questions, and how your offers performed."},"1498":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-55","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#what-it-is","content":"The **People** view lists who registered and who attended. The **Revenue** view breaks down what the webinar earned, separating paid registrations from offers sold in the room."},"1499":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-56","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#what-it-is","content":"For a quick read without opening the tab, the webinar's **Overview** tab shows four live stats (**Registrants**, **Live Attended**, **Total Attended** and **Revenue**) that update as the webinar runs. See The Overview tab."},"1500":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-57","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#what-its-for","content":"Analytics counts how far people get through a webinar, from the page they land on to the offer at the end. Each stage of the funnel is controlled by its own part of your setup. So a weak number tells you which part to work on: the page, the reminders, the talk, the offer or the checkout."},"1501":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-58","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#how-it-helps","content":"**It locates the leak.** **Visitors** to **Registered** measures your registration page. **Registered** to attended measures your reminder emails."},"1502":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-59","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#how-it-helps","content":"**It separates offer problems from checkout problems.** **Views to Clicks** and **Clicks to Purchases** show where buyers drop out."},"1503":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-60","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#how-it-helps","content":"**It shows who to follow up.** **Missed** is everyone who registered and never attended."},"1504":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-61","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#how-it-helps","content":"**It ties money to the webinar.** Webinar revenue sits next to attendance, so you can see what each session earned."},"1505":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-62","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#without-it","content":"Without per-stage numbers, a disappointing webinar is just disappointing. You can't tell whether few people saw the page, the page didn't convert, the reminders failed or the offer fell flat. So you end up changing everything at once. It's easy to rewrite a talk that was fine, when the real problem was that people never turned up."},"1506":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-63","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#why-buyers-care","content":"It matters most when a webinar carries a target. That might be sign-ups for a marketing team, enrolments for a course creator or paid seats for a workshop host. It earns its keep in the days after a session, when you choose what to change before promoting the next one."},"1507":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-64","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#approach","content":"Consider a typical case. A B2B marketing team runs a monthly webinar for prospects, and each session closes with an offer button to book a demo. Registrations rose this quarter, but demo bookings stayed flat. The team has to show where the extra registrants went."},"1508":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-65","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#approach","content":"A common approach is to rebuild the funnel from exports. Sign-ups come from the form tool, attendance from the meeting tool and bookings from the sales calendar, and someone lines them up in a spreadsheet. That can take days each month. Names may not match across three lists, and a person who watched live and then on the recording can be counted twice."},"1509":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-66","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#approach","content":"Every stage up to the demo button happens on the webinar platform: the page visit, the sign-up, the session, the recording and the click. A platform that runs all of those can count every stage for the same webinar, so nobody has to merge lists by hand."},"1510":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-67","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#approach","content":"EasyWebinar's **Analytics** tab does that count for each webinar. Its **Overview** view runs from **Visitors** and **Registered** through **Live Attended** and **Replay Watched**. Further down, **Offers Performance** reports each offer's views and clicks. For this team, that shows whether the extra registrants stopped before the session, during it, or at the demo button."},"1511":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-68","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#approach","content":"The counts are built to avoid double counting. **Visitors** counts unique IPs on the landing page. **Total Attended** counts each person once and files them under **Live only**, **Replay only** or **Both**. How other platforms report on a single webinar is covered in How webinar analytics compares, below."},"1512":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-69","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#open-and-set-period","content":"Open your webinar and click **Analytics**. It opens on **Overview**."},"1513":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-70","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#open-and-set-period","content":"*1 Overview, People and Revenue · 2 Date range and Apply · 3 Funnel metrics.*"},"1514":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-71","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#open-and-set-period","content":"Set the date range and click **Apply**. The range applies to every number on the page, so if a webinar looks emptier than you expected, widen it first."},"1515":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-72","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#read-the-funnel","content":"| Metric       | What it counts                  |\n| ------------ | ------------------------------- |\n| **Visitors** | Unique IPs on your landing page |","table":"table-1"},"1516":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-73","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#read-the-funnel","content":"| Metric         | What it counts  |\n| -------------- | --------------- |\n| **Registered** | Unique sign-ups |","table":"table-1"},"1517":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-74","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#read-the-funnel","content":"| Metric            | What it counts                       |\n| ----------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| **Live Attended** | People who joined the live broadcast |","table":"table-1"},"1518":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-75","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#read-the-funnel","content":"| Metric             | What it counts                   |\n| ------------------ | -------------------------------- |\n| **Replay Watched** | People who watched the recording |","table":"table-1"},"1519":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-76","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#read-the-funnel","content":"| Metric             | What it counts                                                                        |\n| ------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Total Attended** | Unique people, live or replay, split into **Live only**, **Replay only** and **Both** |","table":"table-1"},"1520":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-77","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#read-the-funnel","content":"| Metric     | What it counts                 |\n| ---------- | ------------------------------ |\n| **Missed** | Registered and never showed up |","table":"table-1"},"1521":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-78","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#read-the-funnel","content":"**Live Attended** covers the broadcast only. **Total Attended** counts each person once whether they watched live, on replay or both, which is why it's the number to use when you ask how many people the webinar reached."},"1522":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-79","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#find-the-gaps","content":"Two gaps tell you most of what you need:"},"1523":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-80","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#find-the-gaps","content":"| Gap                            | What it measures       | If it's low, look at                               |\n| ------------------------------ | ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Visitors** to **Registered** | Your registration page | The headline, the form and the promise on the page |","table":"table-2"},"1524":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-81","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#find-the-gaps","content":"| Gap                        | What it measures | If it's low, look at                               |\n| -------------------------- | ---------------- | -------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Registered** to attended | Your reminders   | Confirmation emails and reminders, not the content |","table":"table-2"},"1525":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-82","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#find-the-gaps","content":"**Missed** is the group most worth contacting after a session. Send them the replay."},"1526":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-83","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#engagement-and-offers","content":"Further down the **Overview**:"},"1527":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-84","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#engagement-and-offers","content":"| Panel                  | What it shows                                               |\n| ---------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Offers Performance** | Each offer's views, clicks and purchases, with a click rate |","table":"table-3"},"1528":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-85","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#engagement-and-offers","content":"| Panel                                           | What it shows                 |\n| ----------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| **Views to Clicks** and **Clicks to Purchases** | Where your offer loses people |","table":"table-3"},"1529":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-86","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#engagement-and-offers","content":"| Panel                | What it shows                                        |\n| -------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Revenue by Offer** | Total revenue and payment count, with a details link |","table":"table-3"},"1530":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-87","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#engagement-and-offers","content":"| Panel    | What it shows                                   |\n| -------- | ----------------------------------------------- |\n| **Chat** | Total messages, which you can filter by session |","table":"table-3"},"1531":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-88","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#engagement-and-offers","content":"| Panel                   | What it shows                                           |\n| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Questions & Answers** | How many questions were asked and how many you answered |","table":"table-3"},"1532":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-89","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#engagement-and-offers","content":"| Panel                        | What it shows          |\n| ---------------------------- | ---------------------- |\n| **Registrations by country** | Where your audience is |","table":"table-3"},"1533":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-90","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#engagement-and-offers","content":"Read **Views to Clicks** and **Clicks to Purchases** together. A low views-to-clicks rate means the offer itself isn't landing. A low clicks-to-purchases rate means people want the offer but your checkout or price is stopping them."},"1534":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-91","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#engagement-and-offers","content":"After a busy session, the **Not Answered Rate** on Q&A tells you how many questions you left behind. Those are worth answering in your follow-up email."},"1535":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-92","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#people-view","content":"Switch to **People** to see who registered and who attended. For a full list across all your webinars, with columns such as watch percentage, offer clicked and lead score, plus filters and export, use People in the sidebar."},"1536":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-93","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#revenue-view","content":"Switch to **Revenue**."},"1537":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-94","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#revenue-view","content":"|     | Area        | What it shows                     |\n| --- | ----------- | --------------------------------- |\n| 1   | **Revenue** | The revenue view for this webinar |","table":"table-4"},"1538":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-95","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#revenue-view","content":"|     | Area                                         | What it shows                                                |\n| --- | -------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| 2   | **Total Revenue** and **Paid Registrations** | Everything earned, and the part that came from registrations |","table":"table-4"},"1539":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-96","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#revenue-view","content":"|     | Area                  | What it shows                                                    |\n| --- | --------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 3   | **Revenue by Source** | The split between paid registrations and offers sold in the room |","table":"table-4"},"1540":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-97","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#revenue-view","content":"|     | Area             | What it shows                                                                                                          |\n| --- | ---------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 4   | **Paid Webinar** | Switches the section below to registration payments: completed, pending and abandoned checkouts, and every transaction |","table":"table-4"},"1541":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-98","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#revenue-view","content":"Offer sales appear under **Paid Offer** in the same view, so registration revenue and in-room sales are kept apart. The transaction list shows each buyer's name, email, session, registration date, amount and status, and you can search it and filter by status."},"1542":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-99","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#revenue-view","content":"Transactions show one of these statuses: **Pending**, **Processing**, **Success**, **Failed**, **Canceled**, **Refunded** or **Partially Refunded**. **Checkout abandoned** counts people who reached checkout but didn't pay; they aren't registered. A webinar with no payments shows \"No transactions yet.\""},"1543":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-100","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#what-to-do","content":"| What you see     | What it usually means                  | Where to act                                      |\n| ---------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------- |\n| Few **Visitors** | Not enough promotion reaching the page | Your campaigns and the **Registration Page Link** |","table":"table-5"},"1544":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-101","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#what-to-do","content":"| What you see                       | What it usually means     | Where to act              |\n| ---------------------------------- | ------------------------- | ------------------------- |\n| Low **Visitors** to **Registered** | The page isn't persuading | Registration page builder |","table":"table-5"},"1545":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-102","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#what-to-do","content":"| What you see                   | What it usually means          | Where to act    |\n| ------------------------------ | ------------------------------ | --------------- |\n| Low **Registered** to attended | People forget or lose the link | Reminder emails |","table":"table-5"},"1546":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-103","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#what-to-do","content":"| What you see    | What it usually means           | Where to act                                 |\n| --------------- | ------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| High **Missed** | A large audience still to reach | A follow-up to no-shows with the replay link |","table":"table-5"},"1547":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-104","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#what-to-do","content":"| What you see            | What it usually means   | Where to act                            |\n| ----------------------- | ----------------------- | --------------------------------------- |\n| Low **Views to Clicks** | The offer isn't landing | The offer's headline, button and timing |","table":"table-5"},"1548":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-105","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#what-to-do","content":"| What you see                | What it usually means     | Where to act                |\n| --------------------------- | ------------------------- | --------------------------- |\n| Low **Clicks to Purchases** | Interest without purchase | Your checkout page or price |","table":"table-5"},"1549":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-106","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#what-to-do","content":"| What you see               | What it usually means | Where to act                  |\n| -------------------------- | --------------------- | ----------------------------- |\n| High **Not Answered Rate** | Questions left behind | Answer them in your follow-up |","table":"table-5"},"1550":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-107","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#with-follow-ups","content":"**Webinar Follow-ups** on the **Notifications** tab can go to everyone who registered, only attendees, or only no-shows, which matches the **Missed** number directly. **Attendee Action Follow-ups** send based on engagement and whether someone clicked an offer."},"1551":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-108","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#with-crm","content":"A connected CRM can tag people by the same behaviour Analytics counts: **Registered**, **Attended**, **Missed**, **Watched replay**, **Watched full** and **Clicked offer**, among others. That lets your sales or email system act on what the numbers show. See Connect a CRM and map your webinar data."},"1552":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-109","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#with-offers","content":"**Offers Performance** reports on the offers you build on the **CTAs** tab. Comparing sessions is the clearest way to see whether a change, such as adding a countdown timer, helped."},"1553":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-110","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#with-paid-registration","content":"For paid webinars, the **Revenue** view is where every registration payment and its status appear. See Paid webinars."},"1554":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-111","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#with-replays","content":"**Replay Watched** and the **Replay only** and **Both** splits only fill in if people can reach your recording. See Replay pages."},"1555":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-112","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#who-uses-it","content":"These are typical patterns, shown to illustrate how different teams read the same tab."},"1556":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-113","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#b2b-marketing","content":"A demand generation team runs a monthly webinar and tracks **Visitors** to **Registered** after every promotion change. When the rate drops, they test a new registration page headline before changing anything else."},"1557":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-114","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#course-creators","content":"A creator selling a course through an evergreen webinar watches **Offers Performance** and **Clicks to Purchases**. A healthy click rate with few purchases sends them to the checkout page, not the presentation. See Course creators."},"1558":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-115","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#coaches","content":"A coach running paid workshops checks the **Revenue** view after each session, compares **Paid Registrations** with offer sales under **Revenue by Source**, and keeps an eye on **Checkout abandoned**."},"1559":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-116","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#product-teams","content":"A product team running onboarding webinars cares most about **Total Attended** and **Replay only**, because many users catch up on the recording. A high **Not Answered Rate** tells them to go back through the questions and cover the gaps in their follow-up."},"1560":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-117","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#compare","content":"EasyWebinar's **Analytics** tab follows one webinar from page visits to offer sales and revenue. It reports each offer's purchases next to its views and clicks, and counts live and replay viewers without double counting. You know what made money, not just who showed up."},"1561":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics-118","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/analytics/webinar-analytics#compare","content":"Single-webinar reporting, from each platform's public help docs:"},"1562":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/analyti