","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/getting-started/clone-a-webinar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/getting-started/clone-a-webinar","content":"Cloning makes a new webinar from one you've already built, so you don't set everything up again. In the **Clone Webinar** dialog you choose the type of the copy, give it a name, and tick what should come across: registration pages, schedule, replay settings, embed widgets, polls, offers, email notifications and integration settings. Because a webinar's type is fixed once it exists, cloning is also how you end up with the same webinar as a different type."},"2776":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/getting-started/clone-a-webinar-46","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/getting-started/clone-a-webinar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/getting-started/clone-a-webinar","content":"**Expected result:** a new, independent webinar of the type you picked, carrying the settings and assets you selected, with no registrants, and the original webinar exactly as it was."},"2777":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/getting-started/clone-a-webinar-47","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/getting-started/clone-a-webinar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/getting-started/clone-a-webinar#at-a-glance","content":"|           |                                                                 |\n| --------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| **Where** | **My Webinars** → **⋮** on a webinar's card → **Clone Webinar** |","table":"table-0"},"2778":{"id":"/product-docs/webinars/getting-started/clone-a-webinar-48","page_id":"/product-docs/webinars/getting-started/clone-a-webinar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/product-docs/webinars/getting-started/clone-a-webinar#at-a-glance","content":"|                      |                                                                                |\n| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------