2":4448},"orderedDocs":[[678,"\"Registered\" is a weak signal; **Watched full** and **Clicked offer** are strong ones. Tag them separately so your sales team works the right people first:"],[827,"\"You can only have one event live at a time.\""],[1577,"**A brand-new webinar shows zeros** until registrations start."],[2703,"**A button URL is required on every offer**, paid offers included."],[2601,"**A button**, with its own size, icon, text, colours and the URL it opens."],[3593,"**A camera and microphone are needed to get past the device check,** even if you switch them off in the green room."],[3765,"**A camera and microphone are required to enter,** even if you switch them off afterwards."],[2199,"**A chat that can be open to the room.** With **Everyone**, attendees see and reply to each other. eWebinar's help centre describes its chat as private, not public. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[1892,"**A chat the AI writes for you.** EasyWebinar's **AI Simulation** (Beta) generates chat and questions from a cast with set engagement, knowledge, language and behaviour. StealthSeminar's Chat Replay is built from messages you add or import. More detail in EasyWebinar vs StealthSeminar."],[4071,"**A closing point you control.** EasyWebinar's **Availability** setting closes the replay when you choose. Livestorm's help centre doesn't document a replay expiry setting. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[4364,"**A copy of every sign-up.** EasyWebinar's **Notify admin** sends a copy of each registration to an address you choose. Demio's help centre doesn't document an admin copy of registrations, as EasyWebinar vs Demio shows."],[2512,"**A count of the questions you missed.** EasyWebinar's **Analytics** shows questions asked and answered, with a **Not Answered Rate**. Livestorm's analytics dashboard lists the number of questions. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[728,"**A CRM in the same product.** EasyCRM is EasyWebinar's own CRM and connects to a webinar like any other integration. Demio's integration guide has you connect an outside account in your User settings, and no Demio CRM is documented. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[4068,"**A deadline in days or on a date.** EasyWebinar offers **Expire after days** and **Specific date**. WebinarJam's help centre sets replay access as a number of hours after the live session. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[2698,"**A deadline on the card itself.** EasyWebinar's **Countdown timer** is one toggle on each offer. Demio's help centre documents no countdown setting for its Featured Action call to action. More detail in EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[1021,"**A deadline on the offer itself.** EasyWebinar's offer editor has a **Countdown timer** switch. Demio's help docs describe no countdown on a Featured Action. WebinarKit's offer countdown appears on its product page, not in its help docs. See EasyWebinar vs Demio and EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[2041,"**A documented offer countdown.** EasyWebinar's offer editor has a **Countdown timer** switch. Demio documents its Featured Actions, and Livestorm its in-room link promotion, without a countdown setting. See EasyWebinar vs Demio and EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[3877,"**A library video in use** shows in the **Webinar Video** panel on that webinar's **Content** tab."],[3875,"**A live session you recorded** appears on the **Recordings** tab after the session, named after its webinar."],[3040,"**A live webinar runs at one fixed time** in the timezone you set."],[3876,"**A new document** appears on the **Files** tab with its name, upload date and page count."],[3873,"**A new upload** appears on the **Videos** tab with the **EasyWebinar** badge, and your storage figure at the top of the Library goes up."],[5585,"**A new webinar shows zeros** across all four stats until registrations start."],[5398,"**A priced replay option.** EasyWebinar's **Live + Replay bundle** sells the recording as a second option with its own price. Zoom's replay access is complimentary viewing included with the ticket. WebinarNinja's help centre says multiple pricing levels aren't supported. See EasyWebinar vs Zoom and EasyWebinar vs WebinarNinja."],[2511,"**A public chat with private questions.** EasyWebinar sets chat and Q&A separately, so **Everyone** chat can run beside **Private Q&A**. eWebinar's help centre describes its chat as private, with questions answered through that chat. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[2285,"**A published state**, which decides whether the poll is live."],[2283,"**A question**, the thing you are asking."],[1975,"**A real deadline becomes visible.** Attendees see how long an offer stays open without relying on what they heard."],[1662,"**A real start time.** Unlike **On Demand**, there is still a session to turn up for, which keeps an event feel."],[5577,"**A record of called-off sessions.** EasyWebinar keeps cancelled sittings on a **Cancelled** tab so the webinar's history stays intact. WebinarJam's help centre doesn't document a list of cancelled sessions. Compare EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[2862,"**A recorded copy needs a video.** Simulive and evergreen webinars play a recording, chosen on the **Content** tab."],[3405,"**A recording is required.** Every session plays the video chosen at creation or later on the **Content** tab."],[3220,"**A recording is required.** Simulive and evergreen both play a video; live webinars don't."],[3589,"**A rehearsal room inside the webinar.** EasyWebinar's green room is the full webinar room in a **Not Live** state. Demio's help centre describes a waiting room for attendees, with no presenter green room documented. More detail in EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[1184,"**A replay link that isn't live.** The link only works once the replay page is on, and the page then says it's live. Open it yourself after the session."],[4070,"**A replay page with its own pitch.** **Custom Build** gives the replay its own layout, CTAs and branding. eWebinar's help centre doesn't describe designing a separate replay page. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[1186,"**A reply line nobody reads.** People do reply to webinar emails, so set the reply-to address to an inbox someone checks."],[294,"**A script, not just an outline.** EasyWebinar writes the script in named sections with timings and speaker notes. WebinarJam's AI Agenda Planner generates a webinar agenda. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[4366,"**A sender name you choose.** EasyWebinar's **Sender name** can be you, your company or a client. WebinarJam shows the webinar host's full name as the sender, as EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar sets out."],[534,"**A sending identity you verify.** EasyWebinar lets you verify your own domain for sending, while Demio's technical sender address stays fixed. More in EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[113,"**A separate account for each client.** EasyWebinar's client workspaces give each client their own account that you manage, on its own plan. Demio's team article describes inviting Team Members to your one Demio account. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[1723,"**A session minutes away.** EasyWebinar's **Just-in-time Registration** offers a session starting shortly after someone registers. Demio's help centre and product pages don't document a just-in-time option. Compare EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[2198,"**A shared room or private conversations.** EasyWebinar's **Who can see messages** offers **Everyone** or **Hosts only**. Livestorm's help centre says an enabled chat is public, so everyone in the room sees the messages. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[3183,"**A shared room.** Everyone in a session is at the same moment of the video, so chat messages make sense to all."],[5549,"**A straight route into the room.** **Enter Room** is on the same screen as the stats, so going live doesn't mean hunting for a link."],[3041,"**A weekly webinar runs until you stop it**, unless you set an end date."],[4367,"**A WhatsApp welcome, in Beta.** EasyWebinar's Beta **Welcome Message** on the **Whatsapp** tab sends the moment someone registers. WebinarKit's help centre covers confirmation and reminder texts only, detailed in EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[3033,"**A whole term in one schedule.** EasyWebinar's **Weekly** option sets days, an end date and blackout days at once. In Livestorm, each **Add session** click adds one session a week later. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[4232,"**A YouTube video stays discoverable** unless you've unlisted it on YouTube."],[85,"**Access fits the job.** **Admin** suits people who handle billing and settings. **User** suits people who build and run webinars."],[2607,"**Action is one click away.** Attendees click while their interest is high, without leaving the room to look for a link."],[3895,"**Add Media** is where you choose between hosting a video on EasyWebinar and importing it from YouTube, Vimeo, Wistia or a direct MP4 link. The choice decides whether the video uses your storage. See Video hosting."],[5526,"**Add presenter** adds someone who appears on camera and presents."],[1150,"**Add the behaviour emails** if you have time. The offer-click email comes first."],[3154,"**Add Video** opens two routes:"],[4028,"**After the replay ends**, under **Redirects**, sends viewers on as soon as the recording finishes playing. Point it at your offer, a booking page, or the next step you want people to take. Without it, viewers aren't sent anywhere when the recording ends."],[2668,"**After the replay ends**, under Redirects, sends viewers on to your offer or booking page once the recording finishes."],[1900,"**AI chat varies between sessions; a manual script doesn't.**"],[5090,"**AI drafts the whole set of pages.** **Create with AI** writes the registration, thank-you and waiting-area pages from your script, while Demio's public docs describe no AI page writing. Compare EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[2207,"**AI Moderation and Chat Simulation need Easywebinar Chat.**"],[2182,"**AI Moderation**, available from Pro onward, can answer attendee questions from documents you upload and keep the chat civil. It works with the built-in chat only, and it doesn't replace a human moderator on a live session. It is switched on from the **Chat** screen once set up in the **AI Moderation** section."],[3925,"**AI Moderator documents** are PDF, DOCX or PPTX, up to 25MB each, and the AI Moderator is available from Pro onward."],[2709,"**AI offers use credits**: 1 credit for the offers step."],[2372,"**AI polls use credits.** Generating polls costs 1 credit within a Create with AI build."],[949,"**AI Simulation** builds a cast of simulated attendees, each with their own engagement level, knowledge level, language and behaviour."],[1808,"**AI Simulation**: you describe a cast of attendees, and the AI generates what they say."],[5098,"**AI-written copy needs a read.** Check pricing and what's included before publishing."],[3399,"**All three ways to watch in one webinar.** EasyWebinar offers just-in-time, On Demand and set times together on one page. Livestorm says recurring events can't be set up on-demand, and Demio's public docs show no just-in-time option. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm and EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[842,"**Allow camera and microphone access** for EasyWebinar when your browser asks. If you blocked it earlier, change the site's camera and microphone permission in your browser settings, then reload the page."],[483,"**Allowance.** Your **Wallet** has room for the send. A channel that runs out stops sending until the cycle resets."],[1581,"**An abandoned checkout isn't a registration.**"],[5405,"**An abandoned checkout isn't a registration.** Only a successful payment registers someone."],[3874,"**An imported video** appears with its platform's badge, and your storage figure doesn't change."],[2604,"**An internal title**, which only your team sees."],[2603,"**An optional countdown**, shown on the card."],[2602,"**An optional price**, or a **Free** setting."],[5416,"**Analytics → Revenue → Paid Webinar** lists every transaction with its status. The Overview tab shows the total registrants and revenue."],[1575,"**Analytics is per webinar.** The **People** page in the sidebar is the one that spans every webinar."],[4509,"**As many reminders as your schedule needs.** EasyWebinar adds another reminder with **Create New**. Livestorm documents two reminders by default, one hour and 24 hours before, covered in EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[937,"**Ask for consent.** Turn on **GDPR Compliance** to add a consent checkbox you word yourself."],[2321,"**Ask what you will use.** If an answer won't change what you say next or who you follow up with, cut the question."],[3723,"**Attendance:** the webinar's **Analytics** tab shows **Live Attended** for people who joined the broadcast. See Webinar analytics."],[981,"**Attendee Action Follow-ups** go further: they send based on what someone did, including how engaged they were and whether they clicked your offer. Someone who clicked **Enrol now** and didn't buy gets a different email from someone who left after five minutes."],[2022,"**Attendee Action Follow-ups** on the **Notifications** tab send emails based on what someone did, including whether they clicked an offer."],[2679,"**Attendee Action Follow-ups** send based on what someone did, including whether they clicked an offer. They let you treat someone who clicked and didn't buy differently from someone who left after five minutes."],[1118,"**Attendees get a reason to act.** The thank-you repeats the idea they came for and points at your offer."],[2128,"**Attendees help each other.** In a public chat, people often answer each other's questions before you get to them."],[771,"**Automated attendees** counts people watching simulive and evergreen sessions."],[3524,"**Backstage** is the part of the room for people who are present but not presenting yet. Anyone joining as a co-host or moderator arrives backstage rather than on stage. From there you move them onto the stage when it's their turn, and back off when they've finished. This works the same before and after you go live."],[5340,"**Be on Growth or above.** Built-in checkout and paid webinars start at Growth."],[3673,"**Be signed in as a team member.** Any team member signed in to EasyWebinar can open the room. To bring in a co-presenter or moderator, see The green room and backstage."],[3123,"**Be sure about the type.** The type is fixed once the webinar exists. If you later want an evergreen or live version, you clone it."],[512,"**Broadcasts.** A broadcast is a one-off send to a list, such as a replay link after a webinar or an offer that's about to close. Each one depends on this setup being finished."],[3676,"**Build your polls and offers.** Create polls and offers on the **CTAs** tab. You can keep an offer switched off in the list until you want it."],[1003,"**Build** the webinar with **Create with AI**, choosing the course offer category and **Balanced Approach**."],[2646,"**Button URL** is where attendees land when they click: your checkout, booking page or sales page. Write the button **Text** to match what happens next. \"Download Free Toolkit\" tells people what they'll get; \"Click here\" tells them nothing."],[552,"**Call Integration** and **SMS Integration** (Beta) each have their own tab on **Configurations**, and you set them up the same way as email. Your **Wallet** meters call minutes and SMS (Beta) messages separately from your email allowance."],[476,"**Call Integration** and **SMS Integration** (Beta) have their own tabs, and you set them up the same way as email. Skip both if your first sends are email only, and come back when you need them. Calling is connected here, and your **Wallet** meters the minutes."],[4794,"**Campaign capture is a switch on the hosted form.** EasyWebinar's **UTM Params** records the campaign behind each registration, while eWebinar describes UTM capture as a job for its widgets. More in EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[5581,"**Cancelled sessions stay listed.** They're kept under their own tab so the history of the webinar stays intact."],[695,"**Change integration** swaps the connected tool. **Disconnect** removes it from the webinar."],[1247,"**Change one thing at a time.** Between webinars, keep the schedule steady while you change one email, and keep the same date range. The range applies to everything on the page, so a different one will skew the comparison."],[1903,"**Changes apply when you click Save Changes.**"],[4078,"**Changes to the page design need publishing.** Each of the five pages has its own **Publish** button."],[2819,"**Changing the type.** The type can't be edited on an existing webinar, so a copy of the right type is how you move between live, simulive and evergreen."],[4234,"**Changing the video later** doesn't affect the schedule, pages or registrations."],[3310,"**Charging for access?** Paid registration needs a connected Stripe account. See Paid webinars."],[3122,"**Charging for it?** Paid registration runs through Stripe. Leave pricing on **Free** if you aren't charging. See Paid webinars."],[3032,"**Charging is part of the builder.** Choosing **Paid** in EasyWebinar sends registrants to a Stripe checkout. Demio's help centre says it has no native paid webinar feature and points to Zapier. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[3409,"**Chat Simulation runs one mode at a time:** AI or manual, not both."],[3195,"**Chat Simulation**, under **Engagement**, fills the chat on simulive and evergreen webinars, either with **AI Simulation** or with a scripted CSV in **Manual Simulation**. Only one can be active at a time. See Chat simulation."],[3771,"**Chat, Q&A and Show Attendees are setup controls.** Set them on the webinar's tabs before you go live."],[939,"**Check it on a phone.** Use the device toggle; most registrations come from phones."],[1865,"**Check the preview.** It shows timestamps, names and roles as attendees will see them."],[2785,"**Check you have a recording if the copy will be simulive or evergreen.** Those types play a video. A live webinar's recording is in the Library if **Auto Recording** was on when it ran."],[3674,"**Check your camera and microphone.** The room won't let you past the device check without both."],[212,"**Check your credits.** AI generation uses credits, and your balance is shown at the top right of every step. A full build costs around 23."],[5374,"**Checkout abandoned** counts people who reached checkout but didn't pay. They aren't registered. It is a useful number to watch: a high count points to the price, the checkout step, or a mismatch between the registration page and what checkout shows."],[3591,"**Checks before the broadcast starts.** EasyWebinar keeps you in **Not Live** until you click **Go Live** and confirm. WebinarJam's help centre doesn't document a green room or backstage for presenters. More detail in EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[272,"**Choose a video** for simulive and evergreen webinars, which play a recording."],[3037,"**Choose Paid when you create the webinar.** If you switch an existing free webinar to paid, its registration page keeps the free form."],[5342,"**Choose Paid when you create the webinar.** The price block is added to your registration page at creation. See Choose Paid at creation below."],[1386,"**Clear all** resets every filter. The result count below the table shows how far a filter narrowed the list."],[2699,"**Clicks and purchases in one report.** **Offers Performance** lists views, clicks and purchases for each offer. WebinarJam records sales through two tracking codes that you place on your own pages. More detail in EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[114,"**Client work set up for agencies.** Each EasyWebinar workspace keeps a client's webinars, registrants and settings apart. Livestorm's help centre mentions multiple workspaces only in its HubSpot connection article. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[122,"**Client workspaces are separate** from team seats; adding a workspace doesn't use a seat."],[5073,"**Clone Webinar** can copy registration pages into a new webinar. To try a different registration page on a webinar that's already running, clone it and change the copy."],[1009,"**Clone** the webinar as **Evergreen**, select the live recording, turn on just-in-time and **Chat Simulation**, and let it sell every day."],[843,"**Close other apps that are using the camera**, such as another video-call tool, then reload."],[3595,"**Co-hosts and moderators arrive backstage,** never straight onto the stage."],[3761,"**Co-hosts arrive out of sight.** In EasyWebinar, co-hosts and moderators land backstage and stay unseen until you move them on stage. Demio describes presenters choosing **Go On Stage** to appear immediately, and Livestorm's public docs describe no backstage. See EasyWebinar vs Demio and EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[936,"**Collect what you need.** The form starts with name and email. Add a **Phone** field, or your own custom fields such as the student's current level."],[1815,"**Common questions get answered in view.** A scripted question with an `Admin` reply puts an objection and its answer in front of everyone."],[395,"**Configurations** opens on a row of channel tabs, one for each way the CRM can reach someone:"],[3565,"**Confirm recording.** **Auto Recording Enabled** in the header means the session will be recorded; **Settings → Recording Settings** changes it."],[3311,"**Confirm the type.** A webinar's type can't be changed after creation. If you have a live webinar you want to run this way, see Clone a webinar instead."],[5341,"**Connect a Stripe account.** Payments run through Stripe. You can connect it during the pricing step or from **Integrations → Payment**."],[3678,"**Connect any streaming destinations.** If you plan to stream to YouTube or LinkedIn as well, connect them once under **Integrations → EasyCast** in the sidebar."],[734,"**Connecting needs an account with that service**, and you sign in to it during setup."],[4793,"**Consent can differ from one webinar to the next.** StealthSeminar's GDPR option shows one consent checkbox on all its registration forms. Compare EasyWebinar vs StealthSeminar."],[4792,"**Consent is set on the form you're editing.** EasyWebinar's **GDPR Compliance** switch sits on the form block, with your own wording. Demio adds a default GDPR checkbox through an account setting. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[5595,"**Continue to Green Room** stays greyed out until the room can see a working camera and microphone. If you see \"You can only have one event live at a time.\", another webinar is already live. The camera not detected guide covers device problems."],[5582,"**Converting to paid doesn't add a price to the registration page.** Choose **Paid** at creation instead."],[2864,"**Copies are archived, not deleted.**"],[4929,"**Copy the code from the right webinar.** The Registration Widget sits on each webinar's own **Content** tab."],[5484,"**Create the webinar first.** The Overview tab belongs to a webinar that already exists. Start from Create and schedule a live webinar, Create a simulive webinar or Create an evergreen webinar."],[3314,"**Create with AI** also supports evergreen: set **Type** before generating, then choose the video afterwards. See Create with AI."],[186,"**Create with AI** builds a complete EasyWebinar webinar from a written description. In five steps it writes a slide-by-slide presentation script, fills your registration, thank-you and waiting-area pages, drafts the email sequence, and creates polls and offers. A full build takes about 10 to 15 minutes and uses around 23 credits, and everything it produces opens in the normal editors so you can change it."],[927,"**Create with AI** builds a complete webinar from a description: the presentation script, the registration, thank-you and waiting pages, the email sequence, polls and offers. It takes about 10 to 15 minutes, and everything stays editable."],[2653,"**Create with AI** builds a webinar from a description, and offers are one of its five outputs. Script, Landing pages and Emails are selected by default; click the **Offers** chip to include offers."],[2331,"**Create with AI** builds a webinar from a description, and polls are one of its five outputs. Script, Landing pages and Emails are selected by default; click the **Polls** chip to include polls in the build."],[5058,"**Create with AI** can build your pages as part of a full webinar. After it writes the script, the pages step asks you to choose **AI picks for you**, which auto-selects a template, or **Choose manually** to browse."],[2019,"**Create with AI** writes offers for you. Its **Direct Pitch** positioning is \"offer-focused, repeated CTAs, strong urgency\", while **Soft Pitch** is education-focused with the offer at the end. Whichever you choose, the offers it creates are normal offers on the **CTAs** tab, so you can add a countdown to any of them."],[648,"**Create your tags in the CRM first**, then select them in EasyWebinar."],[299,"**Credits are spent per step.** About 23 for a full build; the script and pages are 10 each."],[4799,"**CRM fields must exist first.** Create the field in your CRM, then click **Refresh** before mapping."],[1901,"**CSV files must be UTF-8**, with commas inside messages wrapped in double quotes."],[649,"**Custom fields must exist in your CRM** before you can map to them."],[4928,"**Customise first.** Use **View & Customize** to change how the widget looks before you copy the code."],[3369,"**Days off stay off.** **Blackout Dates** stop sessions on holidays and any other days you pick."],[1245,"**Deadlines bunch the activity.** A rush just before the replay closes could come from the last call, the deadline itself or both."],[3308,"**Decide how people should be able to watch.** Soon after registering, straight away, at set times, or a mix. The schedule step is built around that choice."],[3568,"**Decide on camera and mic.** You can switch **Camera** and **Mic** off in the green room and still go live, for a session built on slides or video."],[214,"**Decide the webinar type.** Choose **Live**, **Simulive** or **Evergreen** before generating. A webinar's type can't be changed after it's created."],[2786,"**Decide what to leave behind.** Everything is ticked if you choose **Select everything**, but you can untick, for example, the emails if the copy needs new ones."],[3120,"**Decide where the video will live.** Uploading it means EasyWebinar hosts it for you. Importing a link means it stays on YouTube, Vimeo or Wistia. See Which video source to use, below."],[1976,"**Deciding later stops being the easy choice.** A visible time limit gives people a reason to act during the webinar."],[3598,"**Design changes apply as you make them.** Anything you change after going live is visible."],[3768,"**Design changes apply immediately,** including mid-broadcast."],[3763,"**Destinations connected once.** An EasyCast destination is connected once for the account and switched on in the room. WebinarJam has you choose the streaming service for each webinar in its configuration wizard, from YouTube Live and Facebook Live. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[2517,"**Disable removes Q&A for the whole session.**"],[3923,"**Don't delete a video a webinar is using.** The webinar plays it."],[1872,"**Don't impersonate real customers.** A simulated message shouldn't pass itself off as something a real customer said."],[3225,"**Don't remove a video a webinar is using.** The webinar plays it."],[5012,"**Drafts stay private.** **Save** keeps your work, and visitors see nothing new until you **Publish**."],[1661,"**Each attendee's own clock.** Sessions follow the attendee's local time, so you don't have to pick slots region by region."],[1423,"**Each row is one person on one webinar.** Someone who registered for two webinars appears twice."],[702,"**Each webinar feeds its own list.** Integrations are set per webinar."],[4154,"**Easy to swap.** The **Webinar Video** panel changes the video without touching the schedule, pages or registrations."],[3772,"**EasyCast is for live webinars.** Simulive and evergreen webinars play a recording rather than broadcasting."],[442,"**EasyCRM Mail** appears above any provider you add. It carries the **Default** badge and has no **Configure** button of its own, and a connected provider shows a **Connected** badge with its server address. You pick between them with the selector at the left of each row."],[550,"**EasyCRM Mail** is the service listed first under **Select Email service**, marked **Default**. Unlike a provider you add, its row has no **Configure** button. The verification notice sits above the whole list, so verify your domain or address whichever service you select."],[737,"**EasyCRM starts at Growth**, and native HubSpot and Salesforce Pardot sync starts at Pro."],[1004,"**Edit** the script and pages, add UTM capture to the form, and **Publish** the registration page."],[400,"**Email Integration** has four parts. **Email provider** lists your services, **Reply & forwarding settings** decides where replies go, and **Analytics** sits beside those two. **Domains** is a button on the provider list."],[4494,"**Email notifications** can come across when you clone a webinar, so a reminder schedule you have tuned carries into the copy."],[479,"**Email service.** The service you want is selected under **Email provider**, and a provider you added shows **Connected**."],[4517,"**Email stays the main channel.** Text and WhatsApp reminders work alongside email, not instead of it."],[4369,"**Emails are set per webinar.** Each webinar has its own confirmation and its own **Email Settings**; cloning is how you carry them to a new webinar."],[202,"**Emails arrive wired up.** Merge tags are already in place, so dates, times and join links fill themselves in."],[297,"**Emails ready before the event.** EasyWebinar drafts the welcome email, three reminders and two follow-ups. Livestorm's AI drafts emails from an event recording, after the event. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[2206,"**Embedded widgets show to attendees.** Join as an attendee to see one; the admin view shows host tools."],[3770,"**Ending is final.** **End Session** disconnects everyone, and nobody can rejoin."],[2519,"**Ending the session is final.** **End Session** disconnects everyone and nobody can rejoin."],[1728,"**Evergreen only.** Just-in-time is part of the evergreen schedule step. Live and simulive webinars use dated sessions in the webinar's timezone."],[4650,"**Evergreen only.** On Demand is set on the evergreen schedule step. Live and simulive webinars don't have it."],[1726,"**Evergreen sessions that start soon.** EasyWebinar adds just-in-time to the evergreen schedule step. Livestorm's on-demand and automation pages don't document just-in-time sessions. Compare EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[2700,"**Every offer measured.** EasyWebinar reports each offer separately under **Revenue by Offer**. eWebinar's help centre says only one conversion event can be tracked per eWebinar. More detail in EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[5399,"**Every payment in one list.** EasyWebinar's **Paid Webinar** view lists each transaction with its status. Livestorm's help pages describe a Paid column per registrant, with no revenue total for the event. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[1419,"**Every UTM value you capture.** **Source & UTM** filters the table by the campaign that brought each person. Livestorm's registrant export says utm_term and utm_content are not exported. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[2476,"**Everyone** for chat plus **Private Q&A** is a common setup: the room stays sociable, and questions reach you in an orderly queue."],[2149,"**Everyone** is the recommended setting and suits most webinars. Pick **Hosts only** for:"],[304,"**Everything is a draft.** Check pages and emails before you publish, particularly prices and inclusions."],[4152,"**Existing videos work as they are.** If the video is already on YouTube, Vimeo or Wistia, you import the link and use no storage."],[5485,"**Expect zeros on a new webinar.** The four stats stay at zero until registrations start."],[2776,"**Expected result:** a new, independent webinar of the type you picked, carrying the settings and assets you selected, with no registrants, and the original webinar exactly as it was."],[3109,"**Expected result:** a simulive webinar with its schedule, pricing and recording in place, listed on the **Simulive** tab of **My Webinars**, with a **Webinar Video** panel on its **Content** tab."],[2934,"**Expected result:** a webinar with its schedule applied, open in the registration page builder, ready for you to publish."],[3297,"**Expected result:** an evergreen webinar with its schedule, pricing and recording set, a list of upcoming sessions generated on its **Overview** tab, and a registration page ready to publish."],[5215,"**Expired Session** on the webinar's **Settings → General** tab sets where people go if their link no longer works. It's empty by default, so fill it in with a page that tells people what to do next."],[1426,"**Export respects your filters.**"],[4764,"**Export** downloads the filtered list."],[3677,"**Fill in End of Session.** On the **Settings** tab, **End of Session** is where attendees go when the stream ends. It's empty by default, which leaves attendees on a finished webinar."],[1417,"**Filters on how people watched.** EasyWebinar's **Behavior** filter covers attendance, watch time and offer clicks. WebinarJam's registrant filter covers who attended, watched the replay or made a purchase. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[3843,"**Find it in the sidebar.** The Library sits in the main sidebar, alongside **My Webinars**, **Create with AI** and **Integrations**. It isn't inside a single webinar, so anything you add can be reused across your webinars."],[303,"**Five polls per poll step.** Each comes with its question, options and reasoning."],[1729,"**Fixed interval choices.** 2, 15, 30, 45 or 60 minutes."],[1007,"**Follow up** with offer-clickers through **Attendee Action Follow-ups**, and tag them in your email tool with **Clicked offer**."],[699,"**Follow-up matches behaviour.** A no-show can start a replay sequence, while an offer click goes to sales."],[1234,"**Follow-Up SMS** (Beta) and the WhatsApp **Follow-Up Message** (Beta) both send after the webinar ends. They work alongside email rather than replacing it: email carries the detail and the text carries the nudge. You'll need people's numbers, so the **Phone** field has to be on your registration form."],[1267,"**Follow-ups on recorded webinars too.** EasyWebinar drafts the same follow-ups for live, simulive and evergreen builds. Demio's best-practices guide says its Replay Follow-Up isn't available on Automated events. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[2982,"**Free** (selected by default): attendees register without paying."],[3401,"**From live to automated in one switch.** EasyWebinar lists recordings of your past webinars under **Recordings** when you pick the video. EverWebinar can import a past WebinarJam session if the same account has an active WebinarJam subscription. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[3539,"**From the Overview tab.** The **Team & Moderators** panel lists the presenters and moderators who can run this webinar. A new webinar shows \"No presenters or moderators added yet.\" Use **Add presenter** for someone who appears on camera and presents, or **Invite** to send an invitation to join the webinar team."],[4797,"**Full name and Email come first, both required.** Phone, custom fields, consent and UTM capture are options you add."],[4802,"**Full name** and **Email**, both required."],[2483,"**Group similar questions** and answer them together on air."],[5231,"**Guest speakers and moderators by link.** EasyWebinar's **Co-presenter Join Link** and **Moderator Join Link for Live room** let people join without an account. eWebinar's help centre doesn't document presenter or moderator join links, as EasyWebinar vs eWebinar sets out."],[3528,"**Guests arrive quietly.** A co-host can join early, sort out their audio and wait backstage without being shown."],[5183,"**Guests don't need accounts.** A co-presenter or moderator joins with a link, without an EasyWebinar login."],[3588,"**Guests held backstage during the session too.** In EasyWebinar, co-hosts and moderators land backstage and move to the stage and back as needed. ON24's guide describes presenters talking backstage before the webinar starts. More detail in EasyWebinar vs ON24."],[86,"**Guests stay guests.** A speaker on one session joins by link and needs no account."],[116,"**Guests without a login.** EasyWebinar's Co-presenter and Moderator join links bring a speaker into one webinar with no account. Kajabi's account users article covers people who help run the account, each with their own login. See EasyWebinar vs Kajabi."],[3119,"**Have a recording.** A simulive webinar plays a video, so you need one in your library or ready to add. You can add it during setup without leaving the builder."],[3307,"**Have the recording to hand.** Every session plays it. You can upload or import it during setup if it isn't in your library yet."],[650,"**Have your login for that service ready.** You sign in to it during setup."],[2643,"**Headline**: what the attendee gets, in their terms."],[3004,"**Holidays stay free.** **Blackout Dates** skip chosen days without ending a weekly run."],[1893,"**Host replies inside the script.** EasyWebinar's CSV has a **Role** column, so `Admin` lines appear as host replies. WebinarKit's chat simulator documents a username, message text and display time for each message. More detail in EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[4230,"**Hosted files count towards storage; imported links don't.**"],[4222,"**Hosting comes with the webinar.** **Local import** uploads the file and EasyWebinar serves it. EverWebinar's help centre lists an external video as required for its primary video source. See EasyWebinar vs EverWebinar."],[225,"**How long it runs.**"],[2667,"**How long the replay stays up**: **Always Available**, **Expire after days** or **Specific date**. A replay that closes gives the offer a matching deadline."],[3156,"**Import from URL** plays a video already on **YouTube**, **Vimeo**, **Wistia** or a direct **MP4** link. You enter the link and the video's length."],[4231,"**Imported videos depend on the other platform.** Removing a YouTube video breaks the webinar that plays it."],[3223,"**Imported videos need an accurate duration.** EasyWebinar uses it to time sessions."],[3408,"**Imported videos need an accurate duration.** It's how EasyWebinar knows how long each session runs."],[4229,"**Imported videos need their duration entered.** EasyWebinar reads the length automatically only for uploaded files."],[4228,"**Imports come from four sources:** **YouTube**, **Vimeo**, **Wistia** or a direct **MP4 link**."],[2813,"**In My Webinars**, the copy appears with the new name and its type badge, and the count on the matching type tab goes up."],[3167,"**In My Webinars**, the webinar sits under the **Simulive** tab and its card carries a type badge, the next session's date, time and timezone, and the registrant count."],[4074,"**Instant replay is set elsewhere.** **On Demand** belongs to an evergreen webinar's schedule, not to the Replay tab."],[4645,"**Instant viewing that keeps your schedule.** EasyWebinar runs **On Demand** beside a daily or weekly **Recurring Schedule** on one webinar. Livestorm's help centre says that once an on-demand registrant exists, you can't add more sessions. Compare EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[2837,"**Integration settings** carries the original's integration setup to the copy. Check the connections on the copy's **Integrations** tab before it goes live. See Connect a CRM and map your webinar data."],[733,"**Integrations are per webinar.** Connecting one doesn't connect the rest, and different webinars can feed different lists."],[5238,"**Integrations are per webinar.** Mapping join and replay links into a CRM is set up on each webinar."],[2856,"**Integrations come along on request.** EasyWebinar has an **Integration settings** item in the clone dialog. Livestorm's public docs show no copying of integrations. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[1660,"**Interest is still fresh.** The person has just chosen to watch, and a short **Interval** lets them do it while that holds."],[3366,"**Interest meets a session quickly.** With **Just-in-time Registration** or **On Demand**, a visitor doesn't have to come back another day to watch."],[5527,"**Invite** sends an invitation to join the webinar team."],[4312,"**It arrives at the moment of highest interest.** It lands the moment someone registers, while the webinar is still on their mind."],[2288,"**It breaks up a long talk.** A question every so often turns a passive audience into a responsive one."],[407,"**It brings replies back to you.** You choose the address, so a reply reaches someone who reads it."],[4451,"**It brings the session back into view.** A sign-up from days ago is easy to forget. A reminder an hour before puts it in front of the person again."],[4007,"**It can carry a deadline.** **Expire after days** or **Specific date** give the replay a closing point."],[5011,"**It can carry your tracking.** Pixels and analytics scripts go on the page from the builder's settings."],[4006,"**It can keep selling.** With **Webinar Replica**, the replay carries the same offers and polls as the live session."],[2290,"**It can point to buyers.** A question such as \"when are you planning to travel?\" separates people close to a decision from people who are browsing."],[913,"**It catches late viewers.** **After the replay ends** can redirect replay viewers to your course checkout."],[537,"**It covers the CRM only.** Broadcasts and workflows use it. A webinar's own emails, SMS (Beta) and WhatsApp (Beta) use that webinar's **Notifications** tab."],[911,"**It drafts the webinar for you.** **Create with AI** turns one description into a script, pages, emails, polls and offers."],[1353,"**It exports segments, not everything.** **Export** downloads the filtered list, so the work the filters did comes with it."],[4731,"**It feeds your CRM.** The phone number can be mapped into a CRM field of your choice."],[2291,"**It feeds your follow-up.** **People** records how many polls each person answered, next to watch time and offer clicks."],[2131,"**It fits an existing tool.** On recorded webinars, **Third party** keeps conversations in the chat tool your team already uses."],[912,"**It follows up by behaviour.** Emails and email-tool tags can follow who attended and who clicked your offer."],[4313,"**It gives the join link a permanent home.** The registrant can search their inbox for it instead of hunting for your page."],[4008,"**It hands viewers a next step.** **After the replay ends** sends them to an offer or a booking page."],[406,"**It improves your deliverability.** A verified domain gives you better deliverability than a verified single address."],[4454,"**It is measurable.** **Registered** to attended in Analytics shows whether the reminders are working."],[4651,"**It isn't the replay page.** Replay availability, deadlines, redirects and the replay page's look are set on the **Replay** tab for the replay page."],[1501,"**It locates the leak.** **Visitors** to **Registered** measures your registration page. **Registered** to attended measures your reminder emails."],[4727,"**It makes text reminders possible.** SMS and WhatsApp reminders (both in Beta) go to the number someone gave you, so they depend on the **Phone** field."],[1899,"**It needs the built-in chat.** Third-party chat replaces EasyWebinar's panel."],[4315,"**It opens a reply channel.** The **Reply-to email** is an address you choose, so a registrant with a question can simply reply."],[404,"**It opens the gate.** Broadcasts and workflows can go out once a service and a verified sender are in place."],[1813,"**It plays in every session.** On an evergreen webinar that runs all day, the same setup plays each time without you."],[2824,"**It protects what's live.** The original isn't touched, so a working webinar keeps working while you experiment."],[4729,"**It puts consent on the form.** **GDPR Compliance** adds the checkbox with your own wording, so you don't need a separate consent step."],[405,"**It puts your name on the mail.** Your contacts see a domain or address that belongs to your business."],[1351,"**It ranks engagement for you.** **Lead score** rates how engaged each person was, which makes a long list quick to sort."],[4005,"**It reaches the larger audience.** **Missed**, people who registered and never showed up, is the group most worth emailing."],[4453,"**It runs on every session by itself.** Timing is relative, so nothing needs rescheduling when new sessions appear."],[3368,"**It runs without staff.** Nobody needs to present, and Chat Simulation exists for rooms that run unattended."],[3185,"**It runs without you if needed.** The recording plays on schedule whether or not your team joins."],[2822,"**It saves the rebuild.** Everything you've already written and designed can come with the copy."],[1502,"**It separates offer problems from checkout problems.** **Views to Clicks** and **Clicks to Purchases** show where buyers drop out."],[4314,"**It sets the sender early.** The **Sender name** shown here is the one they'll see on every reminder."],[1350,"**It shows behaviour, not just registration.** **Watch percentage**, **Replay watch percentage** and **Offer clicked** separate interested people from casual sign-ups."],[914,"**It shows what sold.** **Offers Performance** and **Revenue by Offer** report each offer's results for that webinar."],[4730,"**It shows which campaign worked.** With **UTM Params** on, you can filter registrants by **Source & UTM** in the People view."],[2289,"**It shows who is in the room.** Ask about their situation and you learn who you are talking to while you can still adjust."],[1503,"**It shows who to follow up.** **Missed** is everyone who registered and never attended."],[4600,"**It sits alongside scheduled options.** Registrants who'd rather turn up for a session can still pick a just-in-time or recurring one."],[5008,"**It starts filled in.** The schedule and countdown are applied when the webinar is created, so the page works before you touch it."],[2825,"**It starts the copy clean.** No registrants come across, so the new webinar's numbers are its own."],[4599,"**It suits people short on time.** Someone with twenty free minutes between meetings doesn't have to fit a session around them."],[4728,"**It tells you who registered, not just how many.** A custom question gives you context before the session starts."],[1352,"**It ties campaigns to attendance.** With UTM capture on, **Source & UTM** shows which campaign produced people who actually watched."],[1504,"**It ties money to the webinar.** Webinar revenue sits next to attendance, so you can see what each session earned."],[4873,"**It travels with clones.** When you clone a webinar, you can bring its embed widgets along."],[1904,"**It's labelled Beta in the app.**"],[2823,"**It's selective.** You choose which assets come across, item by item."],[4872,"**It's the same snippet everywhere.** Copy it once from the Content tab or the Share dialog and paste it into any page."],[3597,"**Joining by link needs no account,** but a person with a team login can also join as a presenter."],[1642,"**Just-in-time Registration** is an evergreen schedule option that offers each visitor a session starting a few minutes after they register, rather than at a fixed future time. You choose how often these sessions come round, from every 2 minutes to every hour. Each just-in-time session runs in the attendee's own local time, so someone who finds your registration page can be watching shortly afterwards."],[2482,"**Keep an eye on Active during the session**, not only at the end, so a quick answer doesn't wait half an hour."],[2032,"**Keep deadlines consistent.** Match the offer countdown, the replay deadline and what your follow-up emails say."],[1873,"**Keep host answers accurate.** An `Admin` reply is read as your answer, so it should be one you'd give live."],[3845,"**Keep live recording on** if you want your sessions to land here. Recording is on by default in the live room, where the header reads **Auto Recording Enabled**."],[2320,"**Keep options short and distinct**, so each one can be read at a glance."],[4484,"**Keep them short.** A reminder needs the time and the link."],[3844,"**Know what uses storage.** Only files uploaded to EasyWebinar count towards your storage. Videos imported from a URL use none."],[938,"**Know which campaign worked.** Turn on **UTM Params** so each registration records the ad, email or post that brought it in."],[2784,"**Know which type you want the copy to be.** You choose it in the dialog, and it is fixed on the new webinar once created."],[213,"**Know your audience and offer.** The prompt drives everything. Have a specific audience, three or four teaching points, a length, a tone, and what you'll sell at the end ready before you start."],[3309,"**Know your audience's hours.** Recurring sessions run in the webinar's timezone, so pick times that work for the people you expect."],[3846,"**Know your upload limit.** Upload video as **MP4**, up to **4 GB** per file. See video and storage limits."],[1825,"**Know your video.** For a manual script, you'll time messages against the recording, so have it to hand."],[5575,"**Known contacts register in one click.** EasyWebinar's **One-Click Registration Link** carries a contact's name and email in the URL. Livestorm's help centre documents sharing the registration page, with no one-click registration link. Compare EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[5184,"**Known contacts skip the form.** The **One-Click Registration Link** registers someone whose details you already hold."],[3916,"**Larger uploads.** EasyWebinar takes video uploads up to **4 GB** per file. WebinarNinja's help centre lists a 2 GB limit for its video files. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarNinja."],[1427,"**Lead score is calculated from engagement.** It's a guide for sorting, not a replacement for the underlying columns."],[1399,"**Lead score** is calculated from engagement: attendance, watch time and interaction. It rates how engaged someone was, for example **Hot**, so you can sort a long list and start with the most engaged people. It's a quick way to prioritise. For the detail, read it alongside **Status**, **Watch percentage**, **Polls** and **Offer clicked** on the same row."],[515,"**Leads.** **Import from EasyWebinar** pulls registrants and attendees across from a webinar, so the people in your webinar records can be sent to once sending works."],[2484,"**Leave time at the end** to clear what's left in Active before you close."],[2857,"**Less to redo after cloning.** EasyWebinar can copy pages, polls, offers and emails in one pass. WebinarNinja's guide has you clone, then update the title, date and time. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarNinja."],[1864,"**Let it breathe.** Real chat comes in bursts with quiet stretches, not one message every thirty seconds."],[1861,"**Line messages up with the video.** A question about a slide should land while that slide is on screen."],[3762,"**LinkedIn company pages built in.** EasyCast lists **LinkedIn** and **LinkedIn Organisation** next to **YouTube** and **Custom RTMP**. Zoom's livestreaming setting names Facebook, YouTube, Twitch and a custom service. See EasyWebinar vs Zoom."],[484,"**List size.** Send to a targeted list rather than everyone, because it helps on both allowance and open rate."],[2988,"**Live + Replay bundle**, to sell access to the webinar and its recording together"],[1019,"**Live and automated in one place.** EasyWebinar can run the same course webinar live, simulive or evergreen. eWebinar runs recorded sessions, so it covers the automated half of a launch. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[2365,"**Live and automated polls in one product.** eWebinar runs automated webinars only, so there is no live poll to launch. Livestorm's help docs don't describe polls in automated events. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[3034,"**Live and recorded in one account.** EasyWebinar offers **Live Webinar**, **Simulive Webinar** and **Evergreen Webinar** in the same dialog. WebinarJam runs recorded webinars in its sister product, EverWebinar. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[1572,"**Live and replay in one count.** EasyWebinar's **Total Attended** shows unique people, split into **Live only**, **Replay only** and **Both**. WebinarJam shows live and replay data separately, and Zoom reports recording views on Webinars Plus. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar and EasyWebinar vs Zoom."],[5587,"**Live Attended** counts people who joined the live session. **Total Attended** adds replay viewers, so it's the larger number."],[1521,"**Live Attended** covers the broadcast only. **Total Attended** counts each person once whether they watched live, on replay or both, which is why it's the number to use when you ask how many people the webinar reached."],[1582,"**Live Attended** is the live broadcast only. **Total Attended** counts unique people who watched live or on replay."],[770,"**Live attendees** counts people joining live sessions in the current period."],[3885,"**Live sessions become reusable content.** You can pick a recording as the video for a simulive or evergreen webinar."],[4648,"**Live sessions in the same account.** EasyWebinar runs live, simulive and evergreen webinars, with **On Demand** on the evergreen ones. eWebinar describes its webinars as running without anyone having to be there live. Compare EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[2987,"**Live webinar price**, the amount each registrant pays"],[3402,"**Live webinars built in.** EasyWebinar runs live, simulive and evergreen webinars from one account. eWebinar's public docs show no live video broadcast, and StealthSeminar streams live video in from YouTube Live or Twitch. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar and EasyWebinar vs Stealth Seminar."],[4233,"**Live webinars don't need a video.** Simulive and evergreen webinars are the types that play one."],[2368,"**Live webinars need manual launches.** On a live webinar, each poll is launched from the **Polls** panel."],[2049,"**Live-room timers are different.** Once you go live, the room header shows **LIVE** with a timer of how long you have been broadcasting. That timer counts up and is separate from offer countdowns."],[3155,"**Local import** uploads a file from your computer, and EasyWebinar stores and serves it. No YouTube or Vimeo account is involved."],[1730,"**Local time applies to just-in-time sessions only.** Other sessions on the same webinar use the webinar's timezone."],[115,"**Logins ready as you add them.** EasyWebinar's **Add user** sets the password when you create the member. WebinarJam's team article says the user must accept an invitation and create a password first. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[4758,"**Make it mandatory if you need to.** You can require the box to be ticked before someone can register."],[950,"**Manual Simulation** plays a chat you script yourself in a CSV, timed against your video."],[1809,"**Manual Simulation**: you write every line yourself, with a timestamp, a name and a role."],[3003,"**Many sittings, one page.** **Add Session**, **Daily** and **Weekly** keep repeat sessions under a single registration page."],[4373,"**Merge tags come pre-filled on AI-built emails.** If you rewrite an AI draft, keep the tags that carry the date, time and join link."],[4492,"**Missed** counts people who registered and never showed up. Add a **Webinar Follow-up** with its audience set to no-shows and include the replay link. In **People**, filter by **Behavior** for no-shows to see exactly who they are, then **Export** the list if you need it elsewhere."],[1525,"**Missed** is the group most worth contacting after a session. Send them the replay."],[3527,"**Mistakes stay private.** Audio checks and false starts happen before the broadcast, not at the top of the recording."],[1863,"**Mix the roles.** Attendee questions answered by `Admin` replies read as a conversation. Attendee messages alone read as a wall."],[3921,"**More storage is an add-on.** **Additional Storage (5GB)**, or **Buy More** beside the storage meter."],[84,"**More than one person can host.** With one shared login, only one of you can be in the live room as host."],[3560,"**Move someone to the stage** when it's their turn to speak."],[3561,"**Move them back** when they're done."],[4237,"**MP4**, up to **4 GB** per file. The **Video Selection** screen lists MP4, MOV or WebM, but the **Upload media** dialog says it supports MP4 files only, so upload MP4 to be safe."],[1894,"**Names in the attendee list as well.** **Attendees on Event Page** adds simulated names to the list attendees see. EverWebinar's help centre covers preloaded chat messages, with no simulated attendee list documented. More detail in EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[5400,"**Native, not a workaround.** Demio's help centre points to a Zapier workflow in place of a native paid webinar feature. EasyWebinar's paid registration is a step in creating the webinar. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[2801,"**New Webinar Name** starts as the original's name with \"(Copy)\" on the end. Replace it with something you'll recognise in your webinar list, especially if both versions will run side by side."],[3006,"**No accidental launch.** The registration page stays private until you click **Publish**."],[3216,"**No add-on licence.** **Simulive Webinar** is one of the three type cards in EasyWebinar's create dialog. Zoom's simulive needs a Zoom Events or Zoom Webinars Plus licence on top of a webinar licence. See EasyWebinar vs Zoom."],[4923,"**No CSS needed.** StealthSeminar styles its embedded widgets through CSS selectors you write. Compare EasyWebinar vs StealthSeminar."],[994,"**No EasyWebinar branding:** the **White Label** add-on removes it."],[4150,"**No extra video host.** With **Local import**, a recorded webinar runs with nothing outside EasyWebinar."],[5182,"**No hunting for links.** Every link for the webinar sits in one dialog, a click from the Overview."],[1871,"**No invented testimonials.** Simulated attendees shouldn't claim results or endorse your product."],[120,"**No invitation email.** You set the password and pass the login on yourself."],[1659,"**No long wait.** A session is always a few minutes away, so nobody has to plan a return visit."],[2370,"**No practical cap on numbers.** Add as many polls as the session needs."],[4598,"**No waiting at all.** A registrant who is ready now can watch now."],[2043,"**No widget to install elsewhere.** eWebinar's countdown to the start comes from widgets you place on your own landing page. EasyWebinar's is a block in its own page builder. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[1119,"**No-shows get a second chance.** The replay email lets them catch up before your deadline."],[1121,"**Nobody gets the wrong message.** Separate audiences mean no one is thanked for a session they missed."],[4801,"**Nothing changes for visitors until you publish.**"],[4371,"**Notify admin needs an address.** It sends a copy of registrations to the admin address you give it."],[4646,"**Now or in a few minutes.** EasyWebinar offers **On Demand** and **Just-in-time Registration** on the same registration page. Demio documents on-demand sessions for automated events, with no just-in-time option. Compare EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[5548,"**Numbers that update as you run.** The stats change as the webinar runs, so you can watch registrations and attendance move."],[2447,"**Off**, when the webinar shouldn't take questions at all."],[1570,"**Offer results.** EasyWebinar's **Offers Performance** shows views, clicks and purchases for each offer. Demio's Featured Action shows clicks and the share of attendees who clicked, and its docs describe no purchase tracking. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[2708,"**Offer revenue and registration revenue are reported separately**, under **Paid Offer** and **Paid Webinar**."],[4076,"**Offers and polls carry over only with Webinar Replica.** A **Custom Build** page has its own layout and CTAs."],[204,"**Offers match your pitch.** You choose how hard to sell, and each offer comes back with a headline, button and link."],[1552,"**Offers Performance** reports on the offers you build on the **CTAs** tab. Comparing sessions is the clearest way to see whether a change, such as adding a countdown timer, helped."],[5521,"**On a free webinar** the panel reads **This webinar is free — attendees register without payment**, with a **Convert to paid** button."],[5522,"**On a paid webinar** the panel shows your pricing title and price, and the pencil edits them. A **Payment Gateway** panel shows the connected Stripe account, and **Manage** opens your payment settings."],[1972,"**On a registration page**, it tells visitors how soon the session begins, which turns \"sometime\" into \"in two days\"."],[1971,"**On an offer**, it tells attendees how long they have to act on what you are selling: a course enrolment, a coaching call, a bonus, a programme."],[4578,"**On Demand** is an evergreen schedule setting that lets a registrant start watching your webinar straight away, with no session to wait for. EasyWebinar also calls it **instant replay**: registrants click a button, labelled *Watch instant replay* unless you change it, and the recording starts. It is a different thing from the replay page on the **Replay** tab, which shows the recording of a session that has already happened."],[1700,"**On Demand** lets registrants watch immediately, with no session at all. Pair it with just-in-time and registrants choose between \"now\" and \"in a few minutes\". The On Demand (instant replay) option has its own page."],[3169,"**On the Content tab**, a **Webinar Video** panel shows the recording you chose. Live webinars don't have this panel."],[2814,"**On the copy's Overview tab**, **Registrants** starts at zero."],[2816,"**On the copy's tabs**, the items you ticked are present: pages on **Content**, polls and offers on **CTAs**, emails on **Notifications**, and connections on **Integrations**."],[2815,"**On the original**, registrants, sessions and settings are unchanged."],[3168,"**On the Overview tab**, the **Sessions** panel lists each sitting under **Upcoming**, **Past** and **Cancelled**. A daily or weekly schedule fills the list from its recurrence. See The Overview tab."],[3170,"**On the registration page**, check the session times and publish the page before you share the link."],[1573,"**One date range for the whole tab.** Set a date range, click **Apply**, and every number on EasyWebinar's tab follows it. WebinarJam filters by webinar, session and event, with no custom date range described."],[5397,"**One flow, no second form.** EasyWebinar registers the buyer as soon as payment succeeds. WebinarJam and EverWebinar send buyers back to a registration form, and their PayPal guide warns that people aren't registered until they complete it. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[4870,"**One less step.** Visitors register where they are instead of clicking through to another page."],[4153,"**One library, many webinars.** You add a video once and reuse it on other webinars."],[1898,"**One mode at a time.** Turning on AI Simulation disables Manual Simulation, and the reverse."],[3884,"**One place for every recording.** Live sessions with recording on land in **Recordings**, with no exporting or uploading."],[5546,"**One place to check before a session.** Schedule, pricing, team and links sit side by side, so a last check takes seconds."],[2044,"**One product for live and automated offers.** An EasyWebinar offer, countdown included, runs on every webinar type you create. WebinarJam handles live sessions and EverWebinar the automated ones, as two separate products. See EasyWebinar vs EverWebinar."],[200,"**One prompt, five deliverables.** Script, pages, emails, polls and offers all start from the same description."],[3735,"**One session can reach more places.** EasyCast sends the same broadcast to YouTube and LinkedIn."],[2364,"**One set of polls for every webinar type.** EasyWebinar's live, simulive and evergreen webinars use the same polls. In EverWebinar, poll results are preconfigured, and no poll statistics come from attendee answers. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[533,"**One setup for a CRM's sends.** EasyWebinar's setup serves CRM broadcasts and workflows, while WebinarJam's third-party SMTP service is described for webinar emails. More in EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam."],[1418,"**One table for every webinar.** **People** sits in the sidebar and spans all your webinars. Demio's People section sits under each event's activity. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[3919,"**Only EasyWebinar-hosted files count towards storage.** Imported URLs use none."],[3406,"**Only just-in-time sessions use local time.** Recurring daily and weekly sessions run in the webinar's timezone, despite the message on the schedule step."],[3766,"**Only one event can be live at a time.**"],[5584,"**Only one event can be live at a time.** Entering a room while another webinar is on air shows a message saying so."],[3599,"**Only one event can be live at a time.** If another webinar is live, **Enter Room** shows \"You can only have one event live at a time.\""],[2030,"**Only use a countdown for a real deadline.** The time shown should match what actually happens when it ends."],[1862,"**Open early.** A message in the first few seconds tells new arrivals the room is active."],[5096,"**Page settings in the builder apply to one page.** The same areas on the webinar's **Settings** tab cover every page, and nothing there applies until you click **Save Changes**."],[991,"**Pages:** every page opens in the drag-and-drop builder, with templates, your fonts and colours, and custom CSS."],[2680,"**Paid Offer — Transaction Success** is sent after a successful purchase, as a receipt-style confirmation."],[3143,"**Paid** charges attendees to register and needs a connected Stripe account. On simulive, pricing comes before video selection, so you set the price before you choose the recording."],[2983,"**Paid**: attendees pay to register. Requires a connected Stripe account."],[1895,"**Part of the webinar itself.** Chat Simulation (Beta) sits on the same **Engagement** tab as chat and Q&A. Demio's help centre doesn't document simulated chat. More detail in EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[3005,"**Payment at sign-up.** With **Paid** selected, people complete a Stripe checkout before they are registered."],[5330,"**Payouts are yours.** Payments land in your own Stripe account, and Stripe pays out to your bank on its usual schedule. EasyWebinar never holds your funds."],[5404,"**Payouts follow Stripe's schedule.** EasyWebinar doesn't hold or pay out funds."],[3934,"**PDF, DOCX or PPTX**, up to **25MB** per file. The AI Moderator is available from Pro onward."],[1422,"**People spans every webinar,** unlike a webinar's own **Analytics** tab."],[2682,"**People** has an **Offer clicked** column, and the **Behavior** filter can combine high watch time with offer clicks to find people who were interested and didn't buy. **Export** the filtered list to work with it elsewhere."],[3200,"**People** in the sidebar can filter registrants by webinar **Type**, so you can look at simulive audiences on their own. See People."],[2345,"**People** in the sidebar has a **Polls** column showing how many polls each person answered, next to **Watch percentage** and **Offer clicked**. Use it to see who took part, not only who turned up."],[4905,"**People** in the sidebar lists every registrant across your webinars. After your test registration, find yourself there to confirm the details came through."],[5379,"**People** in the sidebar lists every registrant across your webinars. Filter by webinar, behaviour or source, then **Export** to work with a list of paid attendees elsewhere."],[4760,"**People** in the sidebar lists every registrant and attendee across all your webinars, one row per person per webinar. Columns include **Name** and email, **Phone** (if you collected it), the webinar and its type, the session, and when they registered. Use **Columns** to choose what appears."],[1002,"**People** in the sidebar shows the individuals behind the numbers across all your webinars, with each person's **watch percentage**, **replay watch percentage**, whether they **clicked your offer**, and a **lead score** for engagement. Filter by behaviour, for example high watch time plus an offer click, and **Export** the list."],[1338,"**People** is a single table of everyone who registered for or attended any of your EasyWebinar webinars. Each row shows one person on one webinar, with what they did: their attendance status, how much of the live session and the replay they watched, whether they clicked your offer, and a lead score for how engaged they were. You can filter the table by webinar, dates, behaviour, campaign source, device or location, and export exactly the segment you need."],[1425,"**Phone appears only if you collected it.**"],[844,"**Pick the right device** in the device check if you have more than one camera or microphone."],[3121,"**Pick your session times and timezone.** Sessions play at the times you set, in one timezone, so choose times that suit the audience you are targeting."],[1185,"**Pitching people who already bought.** That's why the last-call templates above carry a line for buyers. It costs one sentence and saves an awkward reply."],[2322,"**Place buying-intent questions near the offer.** Asking when someone plans to act, just before you present an offer, tells you how ready the room is."],[731,"**Points in the session you choose.** EasyWebinar's **Joined webinar after** and **Left webinar before** let you set the point in the session. WebinarJam's trigger examples include leaving early, evaluated after the session concludes. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[296,"**Polls and offers in the same build.** EasyWebinar generates polls from the goals you pick, then offers in the pitch style you choose. WebinarKit's AI Creator Suite covers scripts, slide decks and avatar videos. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[3767,"**Polls are launched manually** on a live webinar."],[2366,"**Polls are part of the AI build.** EasyWebinar's **Create with AI** can include polls alongside the script, pages and emails. The help docs of Demio, Zoom and WebinarKit don't describe AI that writes polls. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[203,"**Polls have a purpose.** You choose what the polls should achieve. Each one explains why it's there and where it fits."],[2047,"**Polls have no countdown setting.** The **Countdown timer** switch is in the offer editor only."],[2373,"**Polls have no countdown.** The poll editor has a question, response options and **Published**; countdowns belong to offers."],[2363,"**Polls written from your goals.** EasyWebinar's polls step asks what the polls are for, then writes five polls with a note on where each fits. eWebinar's AI drafts interactions from the video transcript instead. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[2836,"**Polls** and **Offers** copy to the new webinar's **CTAs** tab, and **Email notifications** copy to its **Notifications** tab, if you leave them ticked. See Polls and Reminder emails."],[967,"**Polls** help too. A question about the audience, such as where they are now or what they want to achieve, keeps people engaged and tells you who is ready to buy. **Create with AI** can write five polls for you, each with a purpose, such as gauging interest in your offer or qualifying leads."],[5583,"**Presenter and moderator links are private.** Anyone holding one can join your room in that role."],[5235,"**Presenter and moderator links grant access.** Anyone holding one can join your room in that role."],[3596,"**Presenter and moderator links grant that role** to whoever holds them. Keep them private."],[5402,"**Prices are set in US dollars.** Stripe may present a local-currency price to attendees outside the US."],[2986,"**Pricing Title** and an optional **Description**, shown to attendees at checkout"],[2516,"**Private means hosts and moderators.** Attendees don't see private questions."],[2451,"**Private Q&A keeps the room on track.** One attendee's question doesn't set the agenda for everyone else, and you choose what to address on air."],[4151,"**Private videos stay private.** A recording you don't want public can live on EasyWebinar, not on a public site."],[2446,"**Private**, so only hosts and moderators see the questions."],[2450,"**Public Q&A cuts repeats.** When people can see a question has already been asked, you don't answer the same thing five times."],[2445,"**Public**, so attendees can see what has already been asked."],[940,"**Publish it.** The link only works once the page is published."],[274,"**Publish the pages.** A registration link doesn't work until its page is published."],[5094,"**Publishing is per page.** Each of the five pages has its own **Publish** button, and the registration link only works once its page is published."],[1588,"**Questions & Answers** shows how many were asked and answered, and the **Not Answered Rate** shows how many you left behind."],[2449,"**Questions don't get lost in chat.** They sit in their own queue until they are answered."],[2510,"**Questions start in their own queue.** EasyWebinar collects them in the room's **Question** panel. In Demio and WebinarJam, a question is a chat message that the host or a moderator marks as one. See EasyWebinar vs Demio and EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[2513,"**Questions stay in the webinar room.** EasyWebinar's Q&A queue lives in the room on live, simulive and evergreen webinars. StealthSeminar's Q&A is a message box that sends each question to you by email. See EasyWebinar vs StealthSeminar."],[1725,"**Quiet hours you choose.** **Exclude specific time** keeps chosen hours free of just-in-time sessions. WebinarKit's help centre covers just-in-time labels and spacing, with no hour exclusion documented. Compare EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[2201,"**Reachable with chat off.** EasyWebinar's **EW Contact Box** works with **No Chat** and sends questions to an email address you choose. WebinarJam's control panel article covers chat visibility, with no contact form documented. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[273,"**Read every page and email** before publishing, especially anything about price and what's included."],[2609,"**Recorded sessions still sell.** On simulive and evergreen webinars the card carries the pitch, and a countdown can carry the deadline."],[1897,"**Recorded webinars only.** Live webinars have real chat."],[3721,"**Recording:** open **Library → Recordings**. The recording is named after its webinar, with its duration and the date it was recorded."],[3922,"**Recordings appear only if recording was on.** Recording is on by default; check the room header before you go live."],[2863,"**Recordings exist only if auto recording was on.** A live session run with recording off leaves nothing in **Library → Recordings**."],[3217,"**Recordings from your own room.** EasyWebinar reuses recordings made in its own live room. eWebinar builds from imported Zoom cloud recordings. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[3914,"**Recordings sit next to your videos.** In EasyWebinar, **Recordings** is a Library tab beside **Videos**, and it appears in the video picker too. Demio's help centre sends you to the **Schedule** page, filtered to **All Past**, to reach recordings. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[3039,"**Registrant numbers depend on your plan.** Attendee and registration limits differ between EasyWebinar's plans; live webinars are on every plan, and paid registration starts at Growth."],[2860,"**Registrants and attendees stay with the original.** A copy starts with no registrations."],[3042,"**Registrants see the next session only** unless you change the schedule preference."],[1580,"**Registration and offer revenue are reported separately**, under **Paid Webinar** and **Paid Offer**."],[5407,"**Registration and offer revenue are reported separately**, under **Paid Webinar** and **Paid Offer**."],[4904,"**Registration Confirmation** is sent immediately after someone registers, and it carries their join link."],[971,"**Registration Confirmation**, sent the moment someone registers, carries their join link."],[5531,"**Registration Page**, beside **Share**, opens the live registration page so you can see what visitors see."],[5520,"**Registration Pricing** shows whether the webinar is **Free** or **Paid**."],[5542,"**Registrations are counting.** After a test registration, **Registrants** moves off zero and the session row's registration count goes up."],[4513,"**Reminders are set per webinar.** Use cloning to carry a schedule to a new webinar."],[4514,"**Reminders go to registrants.** They are written once per webinar and sent to the people who registered for it."],[3224,"**Removing a linked video at its source breaks the webinar.** If a YouTube video is deleted on YouTube, the webinar that plays it stops working. An uploaded video is contained in EasyWebinar."],[3924,"**Removing a video on YouTube, Vimeo or Wistia** breaks any webinar that plays the imported link."],[1187,"**Repeating your reminders.** The reminder emails you sent before the session were about turning up. Follow-ups should talk about what happens next."],[4077,"**Replay emails live on the Notifications tab**, as follow-ups that include the replay link."],[4054,"**Replay settings** are one of the webinar assets you can bring across when cloning a webinar. See Clone a webinar."],[2838,"**Replay settings** brings the replay configuration from the original's **Replay** tab. See Replay pages."],[1579,"**Replay views are counted separately** from live attendance; someone who did both appears under **Both**."],[1554,"**Replay Watched** and the **Replay only** and **Both** splits only fill in if people can reach your recording. See Replay pages."],[4088,"**Replay Watched** in the webinar's Analytics, and **Replay watch percentage** per person in **People**."],[2707,"**Replays carry offers only with Webinar Replica.** A Custom Build replay page has its own CTAs."],[2371,"**Replays only carry polls with Webinar Replica.** A Custom Build replay page is a separate design."],[482,"**Replies.** **Reply & forwarding settings** points at an address someone reads."],[475,"**Reply & forwarding settings** decides where replies to your email go. Point it at an address someone reads, because people reply to marketing email more than you might expect. A monitored team inbox is a sensible choice for a small business, since replies still get seen when one person is away."],[4365,"**Reply-to set per webinar.** EasyWebinar keeps **Email Settings** with each webinar. Livestorm's reply-to address is the account owner's email, changed in team settings, covered in EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[2284,"**Response options**, the answers attendees choose from. You add or remove them freely."],[2820,"**Reusing a webinar that works.** Pages, emails, polls and offers come across, so a new event doesn't start from blank."],[5576,"**Revenue beside registrations.** EasyWebinar's Overview shows **Revenue** next to **Registrants** and attendance. Demio's help centre doesn't document a revenue figure for a webinar. Compare EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[1571,"**Revenue next to attendance.** EasyWebinar's **Revenue** view splits paid sign-ups from offers sold in the room. ON24's report docs show no revenue figure, and Livestorm's analytics docs show none either. See EasyWebinar vs ON24 and EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[1008,"**Review** **Offers Performance** and **Revenue by Offer**, and adjust the pitch."],[1005,"**Run it live** with recording on. Push your enrolment offer with a countdown at the close."],[3887,"**Safer deletions.** The badge tells you whether a video depends on another platform before you remove anything."],[2150,"**Sales sessions** where attendees shouldn't see each other."],[3182,"**Same delivery every time.** A recording doesn't lose its place, run over or forget a point."],[2031,"**Say what ends.** Use the headline or sub headline to state what expires: the bonus, the price or the enrolment window."],[3333,"**Schedule Preferences** decides how many session choices a registrant sees. With just-in-time and On Demand both enabled, it reads **Display Just-in-time & Instant-replay**. Turn on **Blackout Dates** and pick the days the webinar shouldn't run, such as holidays."],[301,"**Scheduling isn't generated.** Set sessions yourself after the build."],[5580,"**Scheduling Options changes the whole webinar.** For one sitting, use the options menu on that session's row."],[5505,"**Scheduling Options** summarises when the webinar runs:"],[118,"**Seats depend on your plan.** Adding a member costs more only if you have used all the seats your plan includes. Seat and role rules are also listed under team and account limits."],[1824,"**Select Easywebinar Chat** on **Engagement** → **Chat**. Simulated chat works with EasyWebinar's own chat panel; **Third party** replaces it."],[3733,"**Selling happens in the room.** Offers and polls are pushed from the same rail you use for chat and questions."],[1006,"**Send the replay** to no-shows, with the replay set to expire after a few days and **Webinar Replica** keeping the offer on it."],[480,"**Sending health.** Look at **Sending health**, beside **EasyCRM Mail**, before you send through that service."],[481,"**Sending identity.** Your domain or single address has finished verification."],[531,"**Sending is part of the product.** EasyWebinar connects your service directly under **Configurations**, while Livestorm's guide sends your own emails through a Zapier automation. More in EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[541,"**Sends draw on a monthly allowance.** Emails, SMS (Beta) and call minutes are counted separately, so running out of one leaves the others working. The cycle follows your signup date, not the calendar month."],[2151,"**Sensitive topics** where people won't speak openly in public."],[3722,"**Session history:** on the webinar's **Overview**, the session moves to the **Past** tab of the **Sessions** panel."],[5547,"**Session-level control.** You can act on one sitting from its row without rewriting the whole schedule."],[3221,"**Sessions run in the webinar's timezone,** whatever the in-app message on the schedule step says."],[2203,"**Set chat before the webinar.** Chat settings are part of the webinar's setup, not the live room."],[3675,"**Set chat, Q&A and the attendee list in advance.** Who can see chat messages and how Q&A works are chosen on the webinar's **Engagement** tab. Whether attendees can see each other is **Show Attendees** on the **Settings** tab. These belong to the webinar's setup, not the live room, so decide them before the session."],[2515,"**Set Q&A before the webinar.** It's part of the webinar's setup rather than the live room."],[3566,"**Set the look.** Backgrounds, blur, frame overlays and layout are on **Design**. Changes apply immediately, so set them here rather than mid-broadcast."],[271,"**Set the schedule.** The build doesn't schedule sessions for you; set them on the Overview tab."],[1145,"**Set your deadlines.** Decide when the offer closes and when the replay closes, and write both down."],[5045,"**Settings** in the builder's top bar applies to the whole page rather than one block."],[3590,"**Several streams from one room.** EasyCast broadcasts to YouTube, LinkedIn or a custom RTMP destination at the same time, switched on in the green room. Zoom's help centre covers livestreaming webinars to YouTube, with no multi-destination streaming documented. More detail in EasyWebinar vs Zoom."],[5230,"**Short links for any channel.** EasyWebinar's shorter links work in posts, emails and show notes alike. WebinarKit documents its short link as a keyword for its text messages, covered in EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[5229,"**Shorter links from the Share dialog.** EasyWebinar's **Shorten URL's** toggle gives you shorter versions of the webinar's links. WebinarJam's help centre doesn't document a link shortener, as the EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar comparison shows."],[5185,"**Shorter links when you need them.** **Shorten URL's** makes links easier to fit in a post or a text."],[302,"**Simulive and evergreen still need a video** after generation."],[2152,"**Small audiences**, where a quiet public chat looks worse than private conversations."],[1246,"**Small lists swing.** On a list of 50, three extra purchases can look like a big change. Look across several webinars before you rewrite a template."],[4516,"**SMS and WhatsApp come from an EasyWebinar number**, so replies don't reach your phone."],[4515,"**SMS and WhatsApp reminders are in Beta** and only reach people who gave a phone number on your registration form."],[4374,"**SMS and WhatsApp welcome messages are in Beta** and need the **Phone** field on your registration form."],[973,"**SMS** and **WhatsApp** reminders (both in Beta) suit the final reminder before a session, when an email may sit unread."],[5213,"**Social Sharing** on the webinar's **Settings** tab, and **Social Sharing (Open Graph)** in the page builder, control how your link looks when someone shares it."],[1393,"**Source & UTM** only has something to filter if your registration form records it. To set that up:"],[3332,"**Start Date** is the day the schedule begins. Leave **End Date** on **No end date** if the webinar should keep running indefinitely, or set a date for a campaign with a finish."],[3886,"**Storage is visible.** The figure at the top of each tab, and the badge on each video, show what uses your allowance."],[5403,"**Stripe is the payment processor** for paid registration."],[700,"**Strong signals stand out.** **Watched full** and **Clicked offer** sit apart from a plain registration."],[2644,"**Sub headline**: the detail that removes doubt, such as what's included, who it's for or when it closes."],[3567,"**Switch on any EasyCast destinations.** Click **EasyCast** in the top bar and turn **Stream** on for each channel this session should reach."],[735,"**Tags and custom fields must exist in your CRM first.** Use **Refresh** after adding a field."],[729,"**Tags for how long people stayed.** EasyWebinar's **Stayed on webinar at least** and **Watched full** each apply their own tag. Livestorm's HubSpot article describes sending registrant and attendee data to HubSpot. See EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[730,"**Tags without a separate tool.** EasyWebinar's **When**, **Then** and **Value** choices tag contacts directly from the webinar. eWebinar's CRM guide also covers connecting products it doesn't integrate with directly through Zapier. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[5525,"**Team & Moderators** shows everyone who can run this webinar. On a new webinar it reads \"No presenters or moderators added yet.\""],[5095,"**Templates are per page, and switching replaces the layout.** Choose before detailed editing."],[5091,"**Templates come sorted by business type.** EasyWebinar sorts templates by business type, while Livestorm applies one set of design settings to its Detailed and Light pages. More in EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[4930,"**Test it after pasting.** Register once and check **Registrants** on the Overview before you send traffic to the page."],[3564,"**Test Share** with the window or screen you'll actually present."],[2821,"**Testing a change safely.** Try a different registration page or offer on a copy, leaving the webinar that's already running alone."],[4800,"**Text reminders depend on the Phone field.** SMS and WhatsApp are in Beta."],[4795,"**Text reminders need no SMS account of your own.** EasyWebinar's SMS reminders (Beta) come from an EasyWebinar number, while WebinarJam asks you to connect your own Twilio account. Read EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam."],[1182,"**Thanking people who didn't come.** Check who each email goes to before you paste in the words. \"Thanks for joining me\" sent to a no-show undoes the rest of the message."],[3410,"**The AI Moderator is available from Pro onward.**"],[2209,"**The attendee list is a separate setting.** **Show Attendees** is on the **Settings** tab."],[4601,"**The button speaks your language.** **Instant replay text** lets you word the button to match your page."],[2600,"**The card attendees see**: a headline and sub headline, as a text offer or an image offer."],[2123,"**The chat mode** decides whether there is a chat panel, and whose chat it is: EasyWebinar's built-in panel, an external tool embedded in the room, or none."],[1268,"**The click is enough.** EasyWebinar's **Attendee Action Follow-ups** respond to the offer click. WebinarJam's purchase filters need tracking codes in your sales funnel. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[2518,"**The contact box is separate.** Contact box questions go to an email address, not to the **Question** panel."],[2861,"**The copy's type is fixed once created.** Check the summary at the bottom of the dialog before you click **Clone Webinar**."],[5092,"**The countdown is native, not a widget.** EasyWebinar builds it into the page, while eWebinar delivers its countdown through widgets on your own landing page. Read EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[2042,"**The countdown is on the registration page.** EasyWebinar's countdown is a block on the page people sign up on. WebinarJam's help docs describe its countdown on a separate holding page for people who open the live link early. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[2705,"**The countdown is per offer.** Polls have no countdown setting."],[5089,"**The countdown sits on the page you promote.** EasyWebinar adds it to every new registration page, while WebinarJam shows its start countdown on a separate holding page. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam."],[1576,"**The date range covers the whole page.** Widen it if numbers look low."],[1266,"**The first email can go today.** EasyWebinar's follow-ups can send right after the webinar ends. Zoom's follow-up email can be sent 1 to 7 days after the webinar start time. See EasyWebinar vs Zoom."],[4647,"**The full webinar, inside the same event.** EasyWebinar's **On Demand** plays the webinar's own recording from the evergreen schedule. StealthSeminar's in-event choice, Watch Yesterday's Replay, plays the previous session, and fully on-demand viewing is its own event type. Compare EasyWebinar vs StealthSeminar."],[3594,"**The green room broadcasts nothing.** The header reads **Not Live** until you go live."],[3407,"**The interval options are fixed:** 2, 15, 30, 45 or 60 minutes."],[4452,"**The last reminder does most of the work.** In EasyWebinar's guidance, the one fifteen minutes before matters most."],[4073,"**The link is public while the page is enabled.** Anyone with the **Replay Page Link** can watch."],[2520,"**The Not Answered Rate is after the fact.** Use **Active** in the room to see what's waiting while you're live."],[2046,"**The offer countdown is set per offer.** Each offer has its own **Countdown timer** switch."],[2701,"**The offer inside the webinar room.** EasyWebinar pushes the card to attendees from the room's **Offers** panel. Kajabi's webinar funnel can run on any webinar host, such as Zoom, linked into the funnel. More detail in EasyWebinar vs Kajabi."],[5234,"**The one-click link only works for known contacts.** It carries name and email in the URL."],[4924,"**The one-click link sits beside the widget.** EasyWebinar's **Share** dialog holds both, while Demio describes one-click links as part of its CRM integrations. More in EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[121,"**The Owner can't be changed from the Team screen.** Contact support if ownership needs to move."],[1020,"**The pitch happens in the room.** EasyWebinar shows the enrolment offer during the session. Kajabi's Zoom funnel makes the pitch afterwards, through follow-up emails that link to the sales page. See EasyWebinar vs Kajabi."],[2608,"**The pitch keeps working on the replay.** With a **Webinar Replica** replay, the same offer appears on the recording."],[5097,"**The price block is added at creation.** Converting a free webinar to paid later doesn't add it."],[5540,"**The pricing is right.** **Registration Pricing** shows **Free**, or your pricing title, price and a connected **Payment Gateway**."],[300,"**The prompt sets the quality.** Vague prompts produce generic webinars."],[5331,"**The recording can be sold too.** A **Live + Replay bundle** gives buyers a further choice that includes the recording, priced separately."],[3734,"**The recording is automatic.** With recording on, the session lands in your Library without an extra step."],[4652,"**The recording is the webinar's.** An evergreen webinar plays the recording chosen on its video step; change it from the **Webinar Video** panel on the **Content** tab."],[5233,"**The registration link needs a published page.** Publish the registration page before you promote the link."],[4372,"**The registration page must be published.** Until it is, the registration link doesn't work and no confirmations go out."],[2048,"**The registration-page countdown is a page block.** It can be hidden on mobile with **Desktop Only** visibility, styled, or removed like any other block."],[5236,"**The replay link is public while the replay page is on.** Anyone with it can watch."],[2127,"**The room feels alive.** With **Everyone** selected, attendees see each other's messages and can reply to each other."],[1812,"**The room never opens empty.** Messages can appear within seconds of the video starting."],[992,"**The room:** backgrounds, overlays and layout in the live room's **Design** panel."],[2855,"**The schedule can travel with it.** Ticking **Webinar schedule** in EasyWebinar brings the sessions to the copy. Demio says none of the sessions are copied, which leaves a blank schedule. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[5539,"**The schedule is right.** **Scheduling Options** shows the frequency, start date and timezone you expect, and the **Upcoming** tab lists the sittings you meant to run."],[3367,"**The schedule maintains itself.** A **Daily** or **Weekly** schedule keeps generating sessions from its **Start Date**, with no end unless you set one."],[1731,"**The schedule step's timezone message is broader than the behaviour.** Rely on the table above, not the in-app message."],[201,"**The script is presentation-ready.** It comes in named sections, each with a timing and speaker notes, and downloads as a PDF."],[4370,"**The sender name is a display name.** Replies go to the **Reply-to email** you set."],[5329,"**The session earns in its own right.** Every attendee has bought a seat, so the webinar brings in money before it starts."],[3356,"**The Sessions list fills itself.** A daily schedule produces a long run of upcoming sessions with no manual entry."],[3529,"**The stage changes on your cue.** You decide when each person appears, so handovers between speakers look planned."],[3732,"**The start is controlled.** Nothing is broadcast until you confirm **Go Live**, and people in the waiting area are moved in automatically when you do."],[3530,"**The start is deliberate.** The broadcast begins only when you click **Go Live** and confirm."],[1977,"**The start time counts down too.** A countdown on the registration page gives a visitor a reason to register now rather than bookmark the page."],[5541,"**The team is in place.** **Team & Moderators** lists your presenters and moderators instead of \"No presenters or moderators added yet.\""],[3355,"**The timezone reads Attendee's local timezone** when just-in-time is on, because those sessions start shortly after each person registers, in their own time."],[2704,"**The title is internal.** Attendees see the headline and sub headline."],[226,"**The tone you want.**"],[3036,"**The type is fixed.** Clone the webinar and choose another type on the copy."],[3404,"**The type is fixed.** To change an evergreen webinar into another type, or a live one into evergreen, clone it."],[4653,"**The type is fixed.** To offer On Demand for a live or simulive webinar, clone it as Evergreen."],[1732,"**The type is fixed.** To use just-in-time with a webinar that is currently live or simulive, clone it as Evergreen."],[3219,"**The type is fixed.** You can't convert a simulive webinar to live or evergreen. Clone it and choose the new type on the copy. See Clone a webinar."],[3214,"**The video lives with the webinar.** With **Local import**, EasyWebinar stores and serves the file, so no YouTube or Vimeo account is involved. EverWebinar's help centre lists an external video as its primary source. See EasyWebinar vs EverWebinar."],[5579,"**The webinar type is fixed.** It can't be changed from the Overview or anywhere else after creation. Clone the webinar instead."],[305,"**The webinar type is fixed** once the webinar is created, so set **Type** before generating."],[4225,"**The webinar video itself, from a link.** In EasyWebinar, an imported link becomes the video your sessions play. Demio's docs describe YouTube, Vimeo and Wistia URLs for the registration page video. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[4069,"**The whole offer, not one button.** **Webinar Replica** repeats the live video, offers, polls and chat replay. Demio's replay page carries a single Call-to-Action window. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[4925,"**The widget has its own look.** Livestorm's form embed inherits the page's branding, while EasyWebinar's widget is customised on its own. Read EasyWebinar vs Livestorm."],[4927,"**The widget is a form, not the whole page.** When you want EasyWebinar's page to do the selling, send the registration page link instead."],[3769,"**Theme is personal.** Light, dark or system changes your view, not the attendees'."],[736,"**There are 15 integrations**, including EasyWebinar's own EasyCRM."],[3357,"**There is a Live tab** in the Sessions panel next to **Upcoming**, **Past** and **Cancelled**. Evergreen webinars have it; it shows sessions on air at that moment."],[2859,"**There is no in-place conversion.** The type of an existing webinar can't be changed; only a copy can have a different type."],[119,"**There is no per-permission matrix.** Access is set by role alone; custom roles were not available at the time of checking."],[4481,"**They come from an EasyWebinar number**, not your own."],[1244,"**They count people, not emails.** **Replay Watched** tells you someone watched. It can't show on its own which email brought them back."],[4480,"**They need a phone number.** Add the **Phone** field to your registration form, or there is nobody to message."],[2204,"**Third party is for recorded webinars only.** A live webinar offers **Easywebinar Chat** or **No Chat**."],[2205,"**Third-party messages stay in your tool.** EasyWebinar doesn't receive them, so reply from the tool's own dashboard."],[539,"**Three SMTP providers are offered.** They are Amazon SES, SendGrid and Mailgun, and each needs your own account with that company."],[5332,"**Ticket income is kept apart.** **Revenue by Source** separates paid registrations from offers sold in the room."],[1902,"**Timestamps run from the start of the video**, not from the clock time of the session."],[4512,"**Timing is relative to the webinar**, not a fixed clock time. Set it in hours, minutes and seconds before the session."],[4508,"**Timing to the minute.** EasyWebinar takes timings such as *0h 15m 0s before webinar*. Zoom's reminder email offers 1 hour, 1 day or 1 week before the start, as EasyWebinar vs Zoom shows."],[2645,"**Title**: a name your team will recognise in the CTAs list, since attendees never see it."],[5486,"**To charge for registration, have Stripe ready.** Converting a webinar to paid needs a connected Stripe account. Read the warning about converting in Step 4 below before you use it."],[5487,"**To go live, have a camera and microphone.** **Enter Room** checks both before letting you in."],[5560,"**Total Attended** includes replay viewers, and the **Attendee Replay link** sits in the Share dialog. Replay availability and design are set on the **Replay** tab."],[275,"**Tune the offers.** Add a countdown timer to an offer with a real deadline, or adjust the button URL."],[1183,"**Two different deadlines.** The date in your email has to match the replay page's closing date and the offer. Check all three together."],[532,"**Two routes to a verified sender.** EasyWebinar accepts a dedicated domain or a single business address on the same screen, while eWebinar's SendGrid steps run through verification in SendGrid. More in EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[2369,"**Two switches control visibility.** The row toggle in the CTAs list and the **Published** switch in the editor both decide whether a poll is live."],[2706,"**Two switches control visibility**: the toggle in the CTAs list and **Published** in the editor."],[4227,"**Upload MP4, up to 4 GB.** The **Video Selection** screen lists MP4, MOV or WebM, but the **Upload media** dialog says it supports MP4 files only, so upload MP4 to be safe."],[3920,"**Upload video as MP4, up to 4 GB.** The **Video Selection** screen lists MP4, MOV or WebM, but the **Upload media** dialog says it supports MP4 files only, so upload MP4 to be safe."],[3917,"**Uploads and links side by side.** **Add Media** offers **Local import** and **Import from URL** on every tab. WebinarKit says direct uploads apply if your plan includes them. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[3226,"**Uploads count towards storage.** Imported links use none. Extra storage is available as an add-on."],[772,"**Usage resets with your billing period**, so the meters show the current period only."],[1823,"**Use a simulive or evergreen webinar.** Chat simulation isn't available on live webinars."],[4798,"**UTM filtering needs UTM capture.** The **Source & UTM** filter depends on **UTM Params** being on in your registration form."],[1424,"**UTM filtering needs UTM capture** turned on in your registration form."],[4750,"**UTM Params** is a switch on the form block. Once it's on, each registration records the campaign that brought it in."],[538,"**Verification comes first.** Nothing sends until your domain or address is verified, and no setting skips this step."],[3400,"**Video hosting in the same flow.** With **Local import**, EasyWebinar hosts the video itself, so you don't need a YouTube or Vimeo account. EverWebinar's help centre says an external video source is required. See EasyWebinar vs EverWebinar."],[4075,"**Viewers go nowhere at the end** unless you set **After the replay ends**."],[1578,"**Visitors are unique IPs** on your landing page."],[514,"**Wallet.** Email, SMS (Beta) and call minutes each have a monthly allowance, listed with the other limits and defaults. Workflows use more over time than broadcasts, because they keep sending every day."],[1724,"**Watch now, soon or at a set time.** EasyWebinar's **On Demand** starts the recording straight away, beside just-in-time and set times. StealthSeminar's instant choice, Watch Yesterday's Replay, plays the previous session. Compare EasyWebinar vs StealthSeminar."],[1420,"**Watch time as a filter.** EasyWebinar filters people by watch time and offer clicks. eWebinar's help centre doesn't describe filtering people by watch time. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[1550,"**Webinar Follow-ups** on the **Notifications** tab can go to everyone who registered, only attendees, or only no-shows, which matches the **Missed** number directly. **Attendee Action Follow-ups** send based on engagement and whether someone clicked an offer."],[5071,"**Webinar Language**, **Date Display Language**, **Date Format** and **Time Format** on the webinar's **Settings** tab control how the webinar reads to attendees. Set them before you promote, so the registration page and emails match. EasyWebinar doesn't translate your own copy; the page says whatever you wrote."],[4437,"**Webinar Reminders** are the emails EasyWebinar sends to registrants before the session starts. Each reminder has its own timing, set as a length of time before the webinar, so the same reminders work for a one-off session, a recurring schedule or an evergreen webinar. You can add as many as you need from the **Notifications** tab, and Analytics shows whether they are working: the gap between people who registered and people who attended is the reminders' job."],[972,"**Webinar Reminders**, timed relative to the session, so they work on evergreen schedules too. A sensible default is a day before, an hour before and fifteen minutes before."],[224,"**What it covers.** The three or four things you'll actually teach."],[227,"**What you're selling at the end,** and the price."],[540,"**WhatsApp (Beta) isn't on this screen yet.** The **Whatsapp** tab in EasyCRM is marked **Coming soon**."],[4510,"**WhatsApp for the final nudge.** EasyWebinar's Beta **Reminder Message** on the **Whatsapp** tab sends before the webinar starts. WebinarJam's reminders run by email, SMS or voice call, as EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar sets out."],[2161,"**Whether they can see each other**: the attendee list, set with **Show Attendees** on the webinar's **Settings** tab."],[2160,"**Whether they can talk**: chat, set on the **Engagement** tab."],[3720,"**While live:** the header shows **LIVE** with a running timer and the **Recording** badge. With EasyCast on, there's one platform icon per destination."],[2208,"**Who can see messages applies to everything attendees post.**"],[2124,"**Who can see messages** decides whether the chat is a shared room or a set of private conversations with your team. It applies to everything attendees post."],[223,"**Who it's for, specifically.** \"Experienced freelance designers stuck at capacity\", not \"designers\"."],[295,"**Whole pages written from the script.** EasyWebinar writes the registration, thank-you and waiting-area pages in one step. eWebinar's AI rewrites registration page sections one at a time. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[4223,"**Wistia links work as well.** EasyWebinar imports from **YouTube**, **Vimeo**, **Wistia** or a direct **MP4 link**. WebinarKit's help asks for direct Vimeo file links rather than regular Vimeo links, and its built-in hosting is a Pro feature. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarKit."],[3540,"**With a join link.** Click **Share** on the webinar and copy the link for the role:"],[513,"**Workflows.** A workflow is an automated sequence, and webinar follow-up is the sensible first one to build. It keeps sending once published, so it relies on these settings for as long as it runs."],[1147,"**Write the attendee thank-you.** Reuse the replay line, then add the one idea and the offer."],[1148,"**Write the last call.** Make one version for attendees and one for no-shows."],[1146,"**Write the no-show replay email.** It's the shortest, and no-shows are usually your biggest group."],[1149,"**Write the two day-after emails.** Pull one real question from your session for the attendee version, and one strong moment from the recording for the no-show version."],[4757,"**Write the wording yourself.** Say what the person is agreeing to, in your own words."],[4482,"**You build them from templates** grouped by tone, then edit the words."],[5406,"**You can change the price later** with the pencil on **Registration Pricing** in the Overview tab."],[5010,"**You can check the phone layout.** The device toggle shows the mobile version without leaving the builder."],[2129,"**You can make it private.** **Hosts only** turns chat into one-to-one conversations with your team when attendees shouldn't see each other."],[3731,"**You can prepare in private.** The green room lets you fix audio, lighting and screen sharing with nobody watching."],[2452,"**You can see what's left.** The **Active** and **Answered** split in the room, and the **Not Answered Rate** afterwards, show what you didn't get to."],[2610,"**You can see where it loses people.** Separate counts for views, clicks and purchases show whether to fix the offer or the checkout."],[3184,"**You can still be there.** You and your moderators answer questions in the chat while the video plays."],[4483,"**You can test first.** **Send Test SMS** and **Send Test Message** send the selected template to your own number. Pick your country from the flag dropdown rather than typing a dialling code."],[3038,"**You can't schedule a session in the past.**"],[3222,"**You can't schedule a session in the past.**"],[1814,"**You choose how much control to keep.** **AI Simulation** fills a room naturally, while **Manual Simulation** plays exactly what you wrote."],[5009,"**You edit what you see.** Changes happen on the canvas, with a settings panel for the block you select."],[83,"**You know who did what.** Separate logins replace a shared one, which leaves you guessing."],[2854,"**You pick what comes across.** EasyWebinar lists eight items under **What would you like to copy?**, each one optional. StealthSeminar's help centre says its duplicate is a full copy of the original event. See EasyWebinar vs Stealth Seminar."],[2130,"**You stay reachable without chat.** Choose **No Chat** and attendees can still contact you through the contact box."],[4922,"**You style the widget, not the code.** EasyWebinar's **View & Customize** changes the widget's look before you copy it. WebinarJam puts style parameters inside the embed code itself. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam."],[701,"**Your CRM sends the reminders.** A mapped join link gives each contact their own working link."],[1120,"**Your deadline stays visible.** A short last call tells people when the replay or offer closes."],[993,"**Your domain:** the **C-Name** add-on puts webinar pages on your own domain."],[3215,"**Your live sessions become content.** The **Recordings** filter on the video step lists your past EasyWebinar sessions. EverWebinar needs an active WebinarJam subscription to import a live session. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[2200,"**Your own chat tool in the room.** EasyWebinar's **Third party** option takes your provider's embed snippet on simulive and evergreen webinars. Demio's help centre doesn't document embedding a third-party chat tool. See EasyWebinar vs Demio."],[516,"**Your own CRM.** You may prefer to send from the CRM you already use. In that case, skip this setup, since you don't need EasyCRM to run webinars."],[3915,"**Your own live sessions, kept.** EasyWebinar saves recordings of your live webinars straight into the Library. eWebinar imports cloud recordings from a connected Zoom account, and notes that Zoom only surfaces recordings under a month old. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[4224,"**Your own live sessions, ready to reuse.** Recordings of your live webinars land in **Library → Recordings** and appear in the video picker. eWebinar's import route lists recent cloud recordings from a connected Zoom account. See EasyWebinar vs eWebinar."],[4871,"**Your page stays in charge.** The content around the form is yours: your blog post, your landing page, your sidebar."],[1022,"**Your setup comes with you.** Clone a live webinar as **Evergreen** and its offers, polls and emails can come too. Demio's **Create On-Demand** makes a new automated event, but the original settings aren't copied. EverWebinar's import of a past WebinarJam session needs an active WebinarJam subscription. See EasyWebinar vs WebinarJam and EverWebinar."],[5237,"**Your subdomain is in every link.** Changing it breaks links you've already sent."],[5099,"**Your subdomain is in every link.** Changing it later breaks links you've already shared."],[4236,"**YouTube**, **Vimeo**, **Wistia**, or a direct **MP4 link**."],[2619,"*1 All · Polls · Offers · 2 Search · 3 The list · 4 Row actions.*"],[2300,"*1 All · Polls · Offers filters · 2 Search · 3 The list of CTAs · 4 Row actions.*"],[3145,"*1 All · Videos · Recordings · 2 Search and sort · 3 Add Video · 4 Drag and drop · 5 Your library.*"],[3340,"*1 All · Videos · Recordings · 2 Search and sort · 3 Add Video · 4 Drag and drop · 5 Your library.*"],[1378,"*1 Categories · 2 Refinements · 3 Apply Filter.*"],[4754,"*1 Categories · 2 Refinements · 3 Apply Filter.*"],[2995,"*1 Category filters · 2 Template cards · 3 Create button.*"],[5021,"*1 Category filters · 2 Template cards · 3 The create button.*"],[4324,"*1 Channel tabs · 2 Email Settings · 3 An email group · 4 Create New.*"],[4464,"*1 Channel tabs · 2 Email Settings · 3 An email group · 4 Create New.*"],[2792,"*1 Cloning from · 2 Clone into · 3 Choose Webinar Type.*"],[2970,"*1 Frequency · 2 Timezone · 3 Session date and time · 4 Add Session · 5 Schedule Preferences · 6 Continue.*"],[1677,"*1 Just-in-time Registration · 2 On Demand · 3 Recurring Schedule · 4 Availability · 5 Schedule Preferences.*"],[3319,"*1 Just-in-time Registration · 2 On Demand · 3 Recurring Schedule · 4 Availability · 5 Schedule Preferences.*"],[4615,"*1 Just-in-time Registration · 2 On Demand · 3 Recurring Schedule · 4 Availability · 5 Schedule Preferences.*"],[2635,"*1 Offer Style · 2 Countdown timer · 3 Offer Price · 4 Ti