 webinar to YouTube or LinkedIn from here?"],[3103,"Can I swap the recording after people have registered?"],[832,"Can I switch camera or microphone once I'm in?"],[629,"Can I tag no-shows?"],[3511,"Can I take someone off the stage?"],[3104,"Can I turn a simulive webinar into an evergreen one?"],[2100,"Can I turn chat off completely?"],[2425,"Can I turn Q&A off?"],[4283,"Can I turn the confirmation off?"],[4985,"Can I use a different template on each page?"],[3829,"Can I use a recording as the content for an evergreen webinar?"],[4131,"Can I use a recording of a webinar I already ran?"],[1785,"Can I use AI and manual simulation together?"],[2106,"Can I use AI Moderation with an external chat tool?"],[2575,"Can I use an image instead of text?"],[1638,"Can I use just-in-time on a live or simulive webinar?"],[366,"Can I use my own SMTP provider?"],[3098,"Can I use the recording of a webinar I've already run?"],[5165,"Can my links use my own domain?"],[4993,"Can my registration page run on my own domain?"],[3286,"Can one evergreen webinar offer just-in-time, On Demand and set times together?"],[4289,"Can registrants get a text or WhatsApp confirmation too?"],[1792,"Can simulated attendees appear in the attendee list?"],[2427,"Can someone else answer questions while I present?"],[37,"Can someone join a webinar as a presenter without an account?"],[5157,"Can someone register without filling in the form?"],[1099,"Can someone who clicked my offer get a different email?"],[2431,"Can the AI Moderator answer questions for me?"],[3977,"Can the replay stay up permanently?"],[5590,"Cancelled sessions are kept under their own tab so the webinar's history stays intact."],[769,"Capacities as shown in the plan chooser. Plans are billed monthly or yearly. The **Plan** tab under **Settings** meters live attendees, automated attendees and storage."],[1311,"Capture campaign data first"],[4679,"Capture campaigns with UTM Params"],[4109,"Change a webinar's video later"],[4467,"Change its subject, content and timing."],[606,"Change or disconnect"],[72,"Change someone's role from the **Actions** column on their row. The **Owner** can't be changed from this screen; contact support if ownership needs to move."],[3072,"Change the recording later"],[4955,"Change the template later"],[5040,"Change what you need across the panel's **Settings** and **Advanced** tabs."],[4491,"Change your reminders, run the next session, and compare."],[2011,"Changes to the registration page, including the countdown, only reach visitors after you click **Publish**. **Save** keeps a draft."],[9,"Changing roles and ownership"],[4198,"Changing the video doesn't affect the webinar's schedule, pages or registrations, so you can replace a recording with an improved cut while the webinar keeps running."],[3872,"Changing the video doesn't affect the webinar's schedule, pages or registrations."],[2060,"Charge for webinar registration: paid workshops, where the registration-page countdown shows how long is left to register."],[3473,"Charge for webinar registration: take payment through Stripe when people register."],[5257,"Charge people to register for a webinar in EasyWebinar, take payment through Stripe, sell a live-plus-replay bundle, and track every paid registration and transaction."],[2895,"Charging for the webinar"],[3081,"Chat and Q&A"],[2492,"Chat and Q&A are separate controls on the same tab. Chat's **Who can see messages** setting and the Q&A option are chosen separately, so you can run a public chat with private questions."],[3193,"Chat and Q&A are set up on the **Engagement** tab, as on a live webinar. You and your moderators reply in real time while the recording plays. See Live chat and Questions and answers."],[23,"Chat and Q&A moderation"],[3637,"Chat and Q&A settings"],[3270,"Chat choices for recorded webinars"],[2191,"Chat features, from each platform's public documentation:"],[2521,"Chat is a running conversation. Q&A collects questions in a list you work through, and with **Private Q&A** attendees don't see it."],[2181,"Chat is conversation; Q&A is a list of questions. A common setup is **Everyone** for chat with **Private Q&A**: the room stays sociable while questions arrive in an orderly queue."],[2442,"Chat is conversation: greetings, reactions, side remarks, attendees talking to each other. Q&A is a list. Each entry is a question, and your job is to work through the list during or at the end of the session."],[2121,"Chat is open conversation in the room, running alongside your video. It is separate from Q&A, which is a queue of questions you work through and can keep out of sight."],[2212,"Chat is open conversation. Q&A is a queue of questions you answer in order, and you can hide it from attendees."],[2126,"Chat lets attendees respond as you present: say hello, react, ask, and talk to each other. It is how a presenter knows the room is listening, and on a simulive webinar it is how you stay present while your recording plays."],[2158,"Chat moderation preferences sit in the room's **Settings**, under **Preferences**, alongside Q&A moderation and appearance."],[2080,"Chat on simulive and evergreen webinars"],[1749,"Chat simulation"],[3241,"Chat simulation"],[1617,"Chat Simulation"],[3082,"Chat Simulation"],[3269,"Chat Simulation"],[1811,"Chat simulation gives a recorded webinar the feel of an attended session. A greeting in the first seconds, a question a few minutes in and a host reply tell a newcomer the room is active. That impression keeps people watching long enough for the content to work."],[1795,"Chat simulation plays a conversation in the chat of a recorded webinar, so a session doesn't open to an empty room. In EasyWebinar you set it up on a simulive or evergreen webinar's **Engagement** tab, under **Chat Simulation**, in one of two ways. **AI Simulation** builds a cast of simulated attendees and generates their chat and questions. **Manual Simulation** plays a script you write in a CSV, with each message timed against your video. The Chat Simulation section carries a **Beta** label in the app."],[1807,"Chat simulation solves that by playing messages into the chat at set points in the video. You choose how those messages are made:"],[1877,"Chat simulation suits evergreen webinars running just-in-time or on demand sessions, where attendees arrive in ones and twos at all hours."],[1745,"Chat simulation: a chat for attendees who each arrive at a different moment."],[4666,"Chat simulation: a chat for registrants who start watching at different times."],[2222,"Chat simulation: fill the chat on an evergreen webinar, where a shared chat isn't possible."],[3424,"Chat simulation: keeping the chat active when registrants watch at different times."],[2533,"Chat simulation: the simulated chat that pairs with **Private Q&A**."],[3383,"Chat, Q&A, polls, offers, emails and analytics behave as on any other webinar. In **People**, filtering by **Webinar → Evergreen** shows how the automated funnel performs against your live sessions. See Webinar analytics and People."],[4628,"Chat, Q&A, polls, offers, emails and analytics work on evergreen webinars as they do everywhere else. Where viewers watch at different times, Chat Simulation on the **Engagement** tab keeps the chat from looking empty."],[1585,"Check **Offers Performance** for views, clicks and purchases, and **Revenue by Offer** for what it earned."],[351,"Check sending before your first broadcast"],[2528,"Check the **Questions & Answers** panel in **Analytics**. The **Not Answered Rate** shows how many questions were left behind."],[2965,"Check the **Timezone**. It defaults to your account timezone. Your live session runs at the time you set, in this timezone."],[3135,"Check the **Timezone**. It starts on your account timezone, and every session plays at its set time in this timezone."],[3857,"Check the badge before you delete anything on another platform. Removing a YouTube video breaks the webinar that plays it, while removing an Ea