edule for an evergreen build."],[1918,"Create an evergreen webinar: the format where attendees arrive at different times."],[1743,"Create an evergreen webinar: the full setup that just-in-time is one step of."],[2226,"Create an evergreen webinar: the recorded format that offers **Third party** chat and Chat Simulation."],[2875,"Create an evergreen webinar: the schedule options to set on a copy cloned as evergreen."],[4664,"Create an evergreen webinar: the schedule step where On Demand is switched on."],[4532,"Create an evergreen webinar: the schedule where relative timing saves the most work."],[2548,"Create an offer"],[2881,"Create and schedule a live webinar"],[3237,"Create and schedule a live webinar"],[2877,"Create and schedule a live webinar: building a webinar from scratch when there is nothing to copy."],[3471,"Create and schedule a live webinar: set a one-time or recurring schedule and choose free or paid registration."],[3784,"Create and schedule a live webinar: set the session time and registration before you open the room."],[853,"Create and schedule a live webinar: set up the session you'll be entering the room for."],[1035,"Create and schedule a live webinar: the manual build, including the registration template step where the **Education** category sits."],[316,"Create and schedule a live webinar: the manual route, and where to set the schedule the AI build leaves to you."],[2062,"Create and schedule a live webinar: the schedule the registration-page countdown counts down to."],[3610,"Create and schedule a live webinar: the session has to exist and be scheduled before you can enter its green room."],[740,"Create it in your CRM, then click **Refresh**."],[138,"Create with AI"],[1941,"Create with AI"],[4268,"Create with AI"],[5285,"Create with AI"],[270,"Create with AI drafts the content. A few things are still yours to do:"],[199,"Create with AI is for getting from an idea to a webinar funnel you can run, without starting each piece from a blank page. It suits a first webinar, a new topic, or a team that needs a launch-ready draft quickly."],[280,"Create with AI is one of several AI features in EasyWebinar. **Chat Simulation** can use AI to populate the chat on a recorded webinar; see Chat simulation. The **AI Moderator**, which answers attendee questions in the room, is available from Pro onward."],[206,"Create with AI matters most to coaches, course creators and small teams who run their own marketing. It matters in the week before a first webinar, when the setup hours are the main thing standing between an idea and a date."],[795,"Create with AI uses credits, shown at the top right of every step."],[2389,"Create with AI: the full build that writes polls alongside the script, pages, emails and offers."],[5116,"Create with AI: the full build that writes these pages from your script."],[3000,"Creating the webinar does not publish it. Your registration page goes live only when you click **Publish**. Use **Preview** to check it and **Save** to keep a draft."],[1316,"CRM and email tools"],[1462,"CRM and email tools"],[2560,"CRM and email tools"],[3963,"CRM and email tools"],[4270,"CRM and email tools"],[5283,"CRM and email tools"],[721,"CRM features, from each platform's public documentation:"],[698,"CRM mapping brings your registrants and attendees into the system you already work in, without exporting anything. Each contact arrives with a tag that says what they did, so your next step can depend on it."],[4726,"Custom fields let the registration form collect what your follow-up actually needs. That might be a phone number for text reminders or a question about who is attending. It might also be consent, or the campaign each person came from."],[4966,"Custom fields, consent and UTM capture"],[4668,"Custom registration fields"],[5111,"Custom registration fields: phone, your own questions, consent and UTM capture on the form block."],[4941,"Custom registration fields: the fields and consent checkbox the form asks for."],[30,"Customer success teams"],[1321,"Customer success teams"],[1626,"Customer success teams"],[2093,"Customer success teams"],[2416,"Customer success teams"],[2759,"Customer success teams"],[3091,"Customer success teams"],[3279,"Customer success teams"],[3498,"Customer success teams"],[3819,"Customer success teams"],[3969,"Customer success teams"],[4419,"Customer success teams"],[4560,"Customer success teams"],[5149,"Customer success teams"],[57,"Decide on a role for each person. The Roles section below explains the difference."],[2944,"Decide the date, time and timezone you will broadcast in."],[2946,"Decide the webinar type first. **The type can't be changed after the webinar is created.**"],[349,"Decide where replies go"],[2628,"Decide whether to switch on **Countdown timer**."],[417,"DKIM lets the owner of a signing domain claim some responsibility for a message. The sending system adds a cryptographic signature, and the receiver fetches the matching public key from that domain. When the signature checks out, the message is tied to your domain."],[334,"DKIM: a signature on each message"],[418,"DMARC lets a domain owner state policies for validation, handling and reporting, which receiving systems can use. It also brings in alignment, which means the domain in your From address has to match a domain that SPF or DKIM has validated. A policy of `none` requests no specific action on delivery, so it's a gentle place to start."],[335,"DMARC: your policy when checks fail"],[1634,"Do attendees see just-in-time sessions in their own timezone?"],[3102,"Do attendees see session times in their own timezone?"],[377,"Do broadcasts and workflows need separate setup?"],[3097,"Do I have to be in the room during a simulive session?"],[2923,"Do I have to be the account owner?"],[633,"Do I have to connect every webinar separately?"],[4984,"Do I have to customise all five pages?"],[2929,"Do I have to pick a registration template now?"],[4986,"Do I have to pick a template when I create the webinar?"],[1962,"Do I need a separate countdown tool?"],[371,"Do I need an account with the SMTP provider?"],[370,"Do I need EasyCRM if I already use HubSpot?"],[637,"Do I need EasyCRM to run webinars?"],[367,"Do I need my own domain to send broadcasts?"],[4708,"Do I need to publish after changing the form?"],[896,"Do I need YouTube or Vimeo to host my recording?"],[3292,"Do I need YouTube or Vimeo to host the recording?"],[4853,"Do I still need a registration page if I use the widget?"],[3827,"Do imported videos use my storage?"],[4129,"Do imported videos use my storage?"],[1198,"Do it all again after your next session, with new dates and links."],[379,"Do mailbox providers require email authentication?"],[3289,"Do my attendees see times in their own timezone?"],[1635,"Do my daily and weekly sessions follow local time too?"],[2268,"Do my polls come across when I clone a webinar?"],[2769,"Do polls and offers come across?"],[3656,"Do polls appear on their own during a live webinar?"],[2766,"Do registrants come with the copy?"],[4428,"Do reminders work on recurring and evergreen webinars?"],[368,"Do these settings change my webinar reminder emails?"],[1104,"Do webinar follow-up emails need an unsubscribe link?"],[44,"Does a client workspace use one of my team seats?"],[5159,"Does a co-presenter need an EasyWebinar account?"],[3508,"Does a guest presenter need an EasyWebinar account?"],[36,"Does a new team member get an email?"],[4288,"Does a webinar built with AI have a confirmation email?"],[4433,"Does a webinar built with AI include reminders?"],[2576,"Does an offer have to have a price?"],[3505,"Does anything I do in the green room get broadcast?"],[1784,"Does chat simulation work on a live webinar?"],[4852,"Does cloning a webinar copy its widget?"],[2767,"Does cloning change the original?"],[890,"Does EasyWebinar host my course?"],[4125,"Does EasyWebinar host videos, or do I need YouTube or Vimeo?"],[1961,"Does EasyWebinar write the offer for me?"],[1955,"Does every offer need a countdown?"],[1331,"Does Export include only the filtered people?"],[180,"Does it work for simulive and evergreen webinars?"],[1793,"Does it work with a third-party chat tool?"],[45,"Does my client get an email when I create their workspace?"],[378,"Does my custom webinar page domain count for email?"],[3099,"Does my video need to be on YouTube or Vimeo first?"],[2430,"Does Q&A work on simulive webinars?"],[1484,"Does replay viewing count as attendance?"],[3291,"Does the webinar ever stop running?"],[338,"Domain or single address: which to verify"],[1193,"Download the list of registrants and the attendance report from the tool that ran your webinar."],[1849,"Drag the file onto the upload area, or use **Choose File**."],[4165,"Drop your file onto the box, or click it to browse."],[2832,"Each copy starts with no registrants, so every month's figures belong to that month, and the original stays untouched. The full list of items sits under **What would you like to copy?** in the dialog. How this compares with other platforms is covered in How cloning compares, below."],[4465,"Each entry shows its **trigger**, the audience it goes **to**, and its **subject**, so the group reads as a timeline of what registrants will receive."],[56,"Each member needs their own email address."],[2599,"Each offer has:"],[5006,"Each page has a working default, so you don't have to design any of them. If you only have time for two, make them the registration page and the replay page."],[1362,"Each row is one person on one webinar, with columns including:"],[5518,"Each row shows the date, time, timezone and registration count for that sitting. A one-time webinar has a single upcoming session. A daily or weekly webinar fills the list from its recurrence, and a daily evergreen schedule generates a long run of upcoming sessions without you adding any."],[1151,"Each template below is a complete email. Replace the words in square brackets, then cut anything that doesn't sound like you. Any version that promotes your offer also needs the opt-out notice and postal address described under What the law says, below. The examples assume a course offer, and the table further down shows what to swap for other kinds of webinar."],[5373,"Each transaction shows one of these statuses: **Pending**, **Processing**, **Success**, **Failed**, **Canceled**, **Refunded** or **Partially Refunded**. An attendee is registered once their payment succeeds."],[2833,"Each type delivers content differently, but pages, emails, polls, offers and analytics are shared across all three. That's why a clone can carry those assets into a different type."],[94,"Each webinar's **Team & Moderators** panel shows everyone who can run that webinar. **Add presenter** adds someone who appears on camera and presents. **Invite** sends an invitation to join the webinar team. The Overview page explains how presenters differ from team members."],[503,"Each webinar's registration confirmation, reminders and follow-ups live on its **Notifications** tab. Their **Email Settings** button holds the **Sender name**, **Reply-to email** and **Notify admin** settings. So if your reminder shows the wrong sender name, look there rather than in **Configurations**."],[3494,"EasyCast"],[3641,"EasyCast"],[3573,"EasyCast destinations are switched on in the green room, before you go live. Once the broadcast starts, a platform icon for each destination appears in the top bar. Connections are made once, under **Integrations → EasyCast** in the sidebar, and work across every webinar."],[3703,"EasyCast is set up per account, so a destination connected once is available on every webinar. It covers **YouTube**, **LinkedIn**, **LinkedIn Organisation** and **Custom RTMP**."],[3747,"EasyCast multistreaming sends the live session to YouTube, LinkedIn, LinkedIn Organisation pages and custom RTMP destinations, connected once under **Integrations → EasyCast** and switched on per session in the room. Facebook isn't offered as a destination; its RTMP details may work under **Custom RTMP**."],[618,"EasyCRM"],[760,"EasyCRM sending allowance"],[469,"EasyCRM starts at Growth, and plans and add-ons are on the pricing page. You reach it by clicking **EasyCRM** under **Other Products** in the EasyWebinar sidebar, using the same login."],[3024,"EasyWebinar builds live, simulive and evergreen webinars from one create dialog. A live webinar can repeat on a **Weekly** schedule and charge at sign-up through a Stripe checkout. It's simple enough for your first webinar and powerful enough to run your whole funnel."],[1983,"EasyWebinar builds the countdown into the offer card itself. On the **CTAs** tab, the coach opens the programme offer and switches on **Countdown timer**. The bonus goes in the **Headline**, so the card says what ends. Because the timer is part of the offer, it appears in every session that shows that offer. With the replay page set to **Webinar Replica**, the offer carries over to the replay too."],[5018,"EasyWebinar builds the registration page inside the webinar itself. EasyWebinar fills in the date, time, timezone and a countdown when the webinar is created. It also puts a name and email form in place. EasyWebinar keeps templates you've saved under **My Templates**, so each month's workshop can start from her own styled design."],[4183,"EasyWebinar can't read the length of a video hosted elsewhere, and it uses the duration to schedule sessions and work out when the webinar ends. A wrong figure cuts the video short or leaves attendees waiting on a finished one."],[708,"EasyWebinar connects HubSpot on the webinar's **Integrations** tab. The team maps **Watched full** to an engaged tag that alerts the reps, and **Missed** to a no-show tag for the replay sequence. On the **Custom fields** tab they map **Webinar Join Link**, so HubSpot can send its own reminders with each person's link."],[1031,"EasyWebinar connects with Kit (formerly ConvertKit), ActiveCampaign, Mailchimp, Drip, AWeber, Keap, Ontraport, GetResponse, Constant Contact and GoHighLevel, and tags people by what they did in the webinar."],[105,"EasyWebinar gives each colleague their own login, lets a guest present or moderate one webinar from a link with no account, and keeps each agency client in a separate workspace on its own plan. Each person's work stays under their own name, and each client's stays in its own workspace."],[4879,"EasyWebinar gives each webinar a **Registration Widget** on its **Content** tab. EasyWebinar lets you change the widget's look with **View & Customize**, then copy its **Embed Code** and paste it wherever the form should appear. The same snippet sits in the **Share** dialog, next to the webinar's links."],[2458,"EasyWebinar gives questions their own queue, set on the webinar's **Engagement** tab. The team keeps chat on **Everyone**, so the room stays sociable, and sets Q&A to **Private Q&A**, so account questions reach only hosts and moderators. The two success managers join with the **Moderator Join Link for Live room** and answer from the **Question** panel while the product manager presents."],[3580,"EasyWebinar gives you a private green room before the broadcast and a backstage where guests wait, both before and during the session. From the same room you can switch on several streaming destinations at once. You and your guests get ready out of sight, so the session opens cleanly."],[1143,"EasyWebinar gives you each of these controls on the webinar itself. **Email Settings** holds the **Sender name** and **Reply-to email**. Each email has its own subject, content, timing and audience."],[2281,"EasyWebinar groups the things you put in front of an audience under **CTAs**, and there are two kinds. An offer sells something. A poll asks something. Both appear in the room only when you decide to show them."],[92,"EasyWebinar handles both from **Settings**. The agency owner adds the producers and the moderator with **Add user** as **User**, and gives the account manager **Admin**. Each accounting firm then gets a client workspace: a separate account the agency manages, on its own plan. Workspaces don't use team seats, so adding a fifth firm leaves the staff logins as they are."],[920,"EasyWebinar handles both halves of that launch. The creator runs a **Live** webinar with recording on, then clones it as an **Evergreen** webinar. The copy plays the recording at a time each registrant picks. The live original is untouched, and the evergreen copy takes over for everyone who joins the list later."],[2831,"EasyWebinar handles both with **Clone Webinar**. For each monthly kick-off, the coach clones the webinar as **Live Webinar** and leaves **Registration pages**, **Offers** and **Email notifications** ticked. For the in-between version, she clones it as **Evergreen Webinar** and picks her strongest kick-off recording on the copy's **Content** tab."],[1127,"EasyWebinar handles that split on the webinar's **Notifications** tab. She adds a **Webinar Follow-up** for attendees and another for no-shows, each with its own timing. An **Attendee Action Follow-up** covers people who clicked the offer. She also sets the replay to close on Friday, so her emails and the page tell the same story."],[3012,"EasyWebinar handles this as a single live webinar. The team picks **Weekly**, ticks Tuesday and Thursday, and sets the course dates as the **Start Date** and **End Date (Optional)**. Holidays go in as **Blackout Dates**, and every trainee signs up on the same registration page."],[1359,"EasyWebinar handles this in the **People** view. The team filters **Behavior** for high watch time and offer clicks, then adds **Source & UTM** to see which campaign each person came from. **Lead score** sorts the result, and **Export** hands the filtered list to the agents."],[3741,"EasyWebinar handles this inside the live room. EasyWebinar puts co-hosts and moderators backstage when they join, so the student can sort out their audio unseen and come on stage when called. EasyWebinar keeps questions in their own **Question** panel, split into **Active** and **Answered**, and with recording on the session lands in **Library → Recordings**."],[1668,"EasyWebinar handles this on the schedule step of an evergreen webinar. The brand switches on **Just-in-time Registration** and picks a 15-minute **Interval**, so a session is never far away. **Exclude specific time** keeps chosen hours clear, and each session runs in the shopper's own local time. **On Demand** can sit alongside it for anyone who wants to start straight away."],[4607,"EasyWebinar handles this on the schedule step of an evergreen webinar. The team switches on **On Demand**, and the registration page offers an instant start beside any other options. They change **Instant replay text** to wording such as \"Start the explainer now\". A **Recurring Schedule** can stay on for managers who prefer to book a time."],[4321,"EasyWebinar handles this on the webinar's **Notifications** tab. In **Email Settings**, the broker sets the **Sender name** to their own name and the **Reply-to email** to the office inbox. **Notify admin** sends them a copy of each sign-up. The **Registration Confirmation** then goes out at once, with each person's join link."],[4014,"EasyWebinar handles this on the webinar's **Replay** tab. The educator switches on **Enable replay page** and keeps **Webinar Replica**, so the offer and polls play as they did live. **Expire after days** gives the replay a closing point, and **After the replay ends** sends viewers to the programme's enrolment page. A **Webinar Follow-up** to no-shows carries the link."],[2616,"EasyWebinar handles this with an offer card built on the webinar's **CTAs** tab. The company writes a headline for the bundle, sets its **Offer Price** and switches on **Countdown timer**. The instructor pushes the card from the room's **Offers** panel during the pitch. Afterwards, **Offers Performance** shows the bundle's views, clicks and purchases."],[1821,"EasyWebinar handles this with Chat Simulation (Beta) on the webinar's **Engagement** tab. The author picks **Manual Simulation** and uploads a CSV of timed messages. In the script, `Attendee` lines ask about pace and meeting times, and `Admin` lines answer as the host. **Preview Simulated Chat** shows the whole conversation before she saves."],[3536,"EasyWebinar handles this with the green room and backstage. The partners click **Enter Room** and land in the room in a **Not Live** state. Each guest joins with the **Co-presenter Join Link**, waits backstage, and moves to the stage when their topic comes up. The broadcast starts only when a partner clicks **Go Live**."],[3174,"EasyWebinar has three webinar types, and they differ only in how the content is delivered. Pages, emails, polls, offers and analytics are the same across all three."],[1964,"EasyWebinar has two countdowns. An **offer countdown** sits on an offer card in the webinar room and shows how long that offer stays open. A **registration-page countdown** shows how long is left until the session starts. Both are built in, and neither needs a separate timer tool or embedded widget."],[4171,"EasyWebinar hosts the file from then on. Upload **MP4** files up to **4 GB**, and EasyWebinar reads the video's length automatically."],[4160,"EasyWebinar hosts the video itself. EasyWebinar lets her upload the file with **Local import**, then stores and serves it the way Vimeo or Wistia would. EasyWebinar reads the length from the file, so she has no duration to type, and the class sits in her Library ready for any webinar."],[4235,"EasyWebinar hosts them. **Local import** uploads your file and serves it, with no other video host involved. Importing from a URL is an option, not a requirement."],[4214,"EasyWebinar hosts your uploads itself, imports links from YouTube, Vimeo and Wistia, and keeps recordings of your live webinars ready to reuse. Your uploads sit in EasyWebinar's own storage, with no third-party breakage."],[577,"EasyWebinar is the webinar platform built for conversions: live, automated and on demand. You build a webinar with a registration page, emails, polls and offers, run it live or from a recording, and follow up through analytics and your CRM or ours. Keep HubSpot, Salesforce Pardot (Account Engagement), ActiveCampaign, Mailchimp or Kit (formerly ConvertKit), or use the built-in EasyCRM natively."],[2501,"EasyWebinar keeps questions in their own queue, lets you make that queue public or private, and reports how many questions went unanswered. The same Q&A setting runs on live, simulive and evergreen webinars. Real questions don't get lost in the chat, and you can see which ones you left behind."],[3893,"EasyWebinar keeps recordings, uploads and documents in one Library for the whole account. EasyWebinar saves each recorded live session to the **Recordings** tab, named after its webinar, with its duration and date. The team can then pick that recording as the video for an evergreen webinar, so each new manager registers and watches in their first week."],[2297,"EasyWebinar keeps the agency's polls on the webinar's **CTAs** tab, beside its offer of a free audit. The partners run **Create with AI** with the goals \"qualifying leads\" and \"segmenting for follow-up\", then edit the five polls it writes. During the workshop, one partner launches each poll from the **Polls** panel when it fits the talk. After the session, **People** shows how many polls each attendee answered, next to **Offer clicked**."],[5555,"EasyWebinar keeps those details on the webinar's **Overview** tab. **Scheduling Options** and **Sessions** show each month's sitting, and a sitting that is called off moves to **Cancelled**. The team copies the **Co-presenter Join Link** from **Share** for the guest, who joins without an EasyWebinar account. **Registrants** shows sign-ups on the same screen."],[4783,"EasyWebinar keeps your own questions, a consent checkbox and campaign capture together on one form block. Its **Phone** field also feeds SMS reminders (Beta), sent from an EasyWebinar number. You learn who registered and which campaign sent them, on the same form."],[2353,"EasyWebinar launches polls live, runs the same polls on recorded webinars, and can have AI write them from goals you pick. Polls land while the audience is still there, whichever way the webinar runs."],[4060,"EasyWebinar lets the replay close after a set number of days or on a date, repeat the live offers and polls, run as a separately designed page, and report replay viewers apart from live attendees. The session keeps working after the live hour, and you can see who came back for it."],[2190,"EasyWebinar lets you choose whether attendees see each other's messages, embed your own chat tool on recorded webinars, and keep a contact form open with chat switched off. You set the room to suit the session, from an open conversation to a contact form."],[2845,"EasyWebinar lets you choose, item by item, what comes across to the copy. The webinar schedule can come with it, and so can the integration settings. You never rebuild a presentation that already works."],[4912,"EasyWebinar lets you style the Registration Widget inside the app before you copy it, with no code to edit. The Share dialog holds a one-click registration link, and **Clone Webinar** can copy the widget into a new webinar. Your form matches your own site without anyone touching code."],[4500,"EasyWebinar lets you time each reminder in hours, minutes and seconds before the session. You can also add a reminder by text or by WhatsApp, both in Beta. More registrants attend when the reminder arrives at the moment you chose."],[5338,"EasyWebinar makes checkout the final step of signing up. The consultant chooses **Paid** on the pricing step while creating the webinar, and **Register Now** on the registration page then opens a Stripe checkout. EasyWebinar registers a founder only once their payment goes through. It then sends them to the thank-you page, which shows their personal join link."],[3206,"EasyWebinar plays your recording at the times you set while you staff the chat. It hosts an uploaded video itself, plays one linked from YouTube, Vimeo or Wistia, and lists recordings of your past webinars as ready-made content. You record the talk once and spend the session with your attendees in the chat."],[569,"EasyWebinar product documentation"],[567,"EasyWebinar product documentation: the full library, for the steps before and after your first send."],[2033,"EasyWebinar puts a countdown on the offer and another on the registration page itself. The offer countdown works the same way on live, simulive and evergreen webinars. The deadline stays in front of people from sign-up through to the offer."],[2690,"EasyWebinar puts a countdown on the offer card itself and reports views, clicks and purchases for every offer. The same offers run on live, simulive and evergreen webinars in one product. The offer lands at the peak of the pitch, and you can see what each one sold."],[5191,"EasyWebinar puts each of those links in the webinar's **Share** dialog. The producer sends the guest the **Co-presenter Join Link** and a colleague the **Moderator Join Link for Live room**. Both join without a login and wait backstage until they're brought on. The producer turns on **Shorten URL's** for the show notes and emails the **One-Click Registration Link** to subscribers."],[1409,"EasyWebinar puts everyone from every webinar in one table, filters it by what people did and which campaign brought them, and exports exactly the filtered list. Sales gets the warmest leads first."],[1713,"EasyWebinar puts just-in-time sessions, instant viewing and set daily or weekly times on one evergreen webinar. It also keeps chosen hours free of just-in-time sessions with **Exclude specific time**, and runs live webinars in the same product. Sessions start minutes after someone registers, in their own time zone."],[5221,"EasyWebinar puts one-click registration, join links for co-presenters and moderators, and a toggle for shorter links in the same Share dialog. Every link you need to send is in one dialog, so nobody hunts for the right one."],[413,"EasyWebinar puts that job on one screen, **Configurations**, inside its CRM. It lists your email services, asks you to verify a domain or a single business address, and lets you choose where replies go. The garden centre's admin could validate the office address for Monday's send and plan the domain work for when volume grows."],[4737,"EasyWebinar puts those options on the registration form block itself. EasyWebinar lets you add custom fields and a **Phone** field, turn on **GDPR Compliance** with your own wording, and turn on **UTM Params**. What people enter then shows up in the **People** view, ready to filter and export."],[4238,"EasyWebinar reads the length of an uploaded file automatically, but not of one hosted elsewhere. It needs the duration to schedule sessions correctly."],[3159,"EasyWebinar reads the length of an uploaded file itself, but not of a linked one. It uses the duration to schedule sessions and to know when the webinar ends, so a wrong figure can cut the video short or leave attendees waiting after it has finished."],[3906,"EasyWebinar records your live sessions into the same Library that holds your uploads and imported links. Any of those recordings can then become the video for a simulive or evergreen webinar."],[1010,"EasyWebinar runs the webinar that sells your course, live or automated, in one product. The enrolment offer appears inside the room, and it can carry a countdown. Your course stays where it's hosted, and EasyWebinar is the conversion layer in front of it."],[3191,"EasyWebinar runs this as one simulive webinar. The school records its strongest taster session, uploads it with **Local import**, and sets a **Weekly** schedule for Saturday and Wednesday. A teacher joins each sitting's chat and answers questions about levels, class times and placement while the recording plays."],[1024,"EasyWebinar sells your course; it doesn't host or deliver it. Lessons, student logins and course progress stay on your course platform. The offer button and replay redirect send buyers there."],[1256,"EasyWebinar sends one follow-up to attendees and another to no-shows, and a further email when someone clicks your offer. Its built-in CRM can then run a longer sequence under the same login. Every attendee gets the next message their behaviour earned."],[4460,"EasyWebinar sets each reminder as time before the webinar, on the **Notifications** tab. The school keeps three: a day, an hour and fifteen minutes before. Each one follows every session on the evergreen schedule. For the final nudge, the school adds a **Reminder SMS**, in Beta, because its audience reads texts quickly."],[521,"EasyWebinar sets the email service, the sending identity and the reply address on one screen in its own CRM. Those settings then serve broadcasts and workflows, with calling on the next tab. And it's your CRM or ours: keep the CRM you have, or use EasyCRM natively."],[2137,"EasyWebinar sets this on the webinar's **Engagement** tab before the session. The firm keeps **Easywebinar Chat** and sets **Who can see messages** to **Hosts only**. Each attendee then talks privately to the team, and nobody sees anyone else. The colleague joins with the **Moderator Join Link for Live room** and answers from the **Chat** panel in the room."],[720,"EasyWebinar tags contacts by what they did in the session, sends each person's join link into a CRM field, and offers its own CRM, EasyCRM, that connects the same way. And it's your CRM or ours: keep the CRM you have, or use EasyCRM natively."],[5387,"EasyWebinar takes payment as part of sign-up: **Register Now** opens a Stripe checkout, and the person is registered once they've paid. It can also sell the replay at its own price, and it lists every payment against the webinar. The sale, the attendee and the data stay in one place."],[210,"EasyWebinar turns her description into a complete webinar through **Create with AI**. She sets **Type** to **Live**, adds the **Polls** and **Offers** chips and clicks **Generate**. The script comes first, and the pages are written from it. She chooses **Balanced Approach** for the offer and downloads the script as a PDF to rehearse."],[3375,"EasyWebinar turns that recording into one evergreen webinar with a single schedule. The team keeps its Tuesday slot as a **Weekly** **Recurring Schedule** and switches on **Just-in-time Registration** beside it. The registration page offers both as choices, so the Wednesday prospect can take a session that begins minutes later instead of next week."],[1510,"EasyWebinar's **Analytics** tab does that count for each webinar. Its **Overview** view runs from **Visitors** and **Registered** through **Live Attended** and **Replay Watched**. Further down, **Offers Performance** reports each offer's views and clicks. For this team, that shows whether the extra registrants stopped before the session, during it, or at the demo button."],[1560,"EasyWebinar's **Analytics** tab follows one webinar from page visits to offer sales and revenue. It reports each offer's purchases next to its views and clicks, and counts live and replay viewers without double counting. You know what made money, not just who showed up."],[5079,"EasyWebinar's builder starts you from a ready-made template, can have AI write the page copy from your script, and puts a countdown on the registration page itself. You get a finished registration page without starting from a blank screen."],[1884,"EasyWebinar's Chat Simulation (Beta) can write the chat with AI or play a script you upload as a CSV. It can also add simulated names to the attendee list. You set the cast or the script yourself, so keep it honest: never present an automated webinar as live."],[4356,"EasyWebinar's confirmation goes out from a sender name and reply-to address you set for each webinar, and **Notify admin** can copy every registration to your inbox. A WhatsApp welcome message, in Beta, can go out at the same moment. Registrants hear from a name they recognise, and you see each sign-up as it happens."],[286,"EasyWebinar's Create with AI writes the presentation script, the registration pages, the email sequence, and the polls and offers from one description. You get a first draft of the whole funnel from one description, and you can edit all of it."],[435,"EasyWebinar's guidance is that a verified domain is worth the DNS work if you send in any volume. If your first send is a small list and it's due soon, the single address is the quicker way to start. Neither route can promise that a given message lands in the inbox, since the receiving mail system makes that decision. For the wider picture, our guide to webinar email marketing covers what happens after your mail is sending."],[3753,"EasyWebinar's live room gives you a private green room, a backstage for co-hosts, and streaming out to YouTube and LinkedIn from the same screen you present from. You run the room like a launch, without leaving the screen you present from."],[4636,"EasyWebinar's On Demand puts a watch-now button on the same registration page as just-in-time sessions and set daily or weekly times. You also choose the button's wording with **Instant replay text**, and you run live webinars in the same product. Each registrant picks the way of watching that suits them."],[5567,"EasyWebinar's Overview gives each webinar private join links for guest presenters, a one-click registration link for known contacts and a **Revenue** figure. Sessions that are called off stay on their own **Cancelled** tab. A webinar's links and its results sit together on one tab, so nothing needs hunting down."],[4404,"Edit a reminder"],[4958,"Edit blocks"],[5385,"Educators in fields such as real estate, finance or wellness run paid seminars. Paid registration keeps the attendee list limited to people who paid, and the transaction list gives a record of every purchase."],[1584,"Either the webinar hasn't run yet, or your date range doesn't cover the period when it did."],[3158,"Either way, the video is saved to your library and can be reused on other webinars. For the full upload and import walkthrough, see Video hosting."],[739,"Eleven, from **Registered** to **Clicked offer**. Each mapping applies the tag you choose when its event fires."],[1286,"Email Subject Lines: 5 Tips to Attract Readers, Nielsen Norman Group, 2014: why useful words go first, and why names and symbols rarely help."],[162,"Emails"],[4557,"Emails"],[5282,"Emails"],[1619,"Emails and reminders"],[3083,"Emails and reminders"],[3272,"Emails and reminders"],[2083,"Embed a third-party chat tool"],[4967,"Embedding the form on your own site"],[2485,"Ending the session disconnects everyone and nobody can rejoin, so finish the questions you want to answer before you click **End Session**."],[2910,"Engagement in the room"],[4336,"Enter a **Reply-to email**."],[4335,"Enter a **Sender name**."],[4176,"Enter the **Video duration** in hours, minutes and seconds."],[3315,"Enter the **Webinar Name** your registrants will see."],[3615,"Enter the EasyWebinar webinar room, prepare in the green room, go live, present with chat, polls, offers and Q&A, then end the session and find your recording."],[2327,"Enter the room from the webinar's **Overview** with **Enter Room**."],[847,"Enter the room well before your start time. The green room broadcasts nothing, so you can pass the device check, finish your checks and test **Share** before anyone is watching. Close other video-call tools before you click **Enter Room**, so nothing else is holding the camera. For the kit itself, see the webinar equipment guide and this host preparation guide."],[63,"Enter their **Name** and **Email**, and optionally a **Photo**."],[5440,"Entering a running session on a recorded webinar"],[3431,"Evergreen"],[4411,"Evergreen and just-in-time sessions"],[3391,"Evergreen features, from each platform's public documentation:"],[3640,"Evergreen from a live session"],[5289,"Evergreen paid trainings"],[1772,"Evergreen schedules"],[3365,"Evergreen suits a webinar that belongs to a funnel and should work whether or not you're free. Typical examples are a product demo, customer onboarding or a year-round offer. People reach it at all hours, so it has to be ready whenever they do."],[3379,"Evergreen webinars can use **Easywebinar Chat**, embed an external chat tool with **Third party**, or turn chat off with **No Chat** while keeping the **EW Contact Box** for questions sent by email."],[1702,"Evergreen webinars have a **Live** tab in the Sessions panel, alongside **Upcoming**, **Past** and **Cancelled**, showing sessions currently on air. The webinar Overview tab explains the rest of that screen."],[2082,"Evergreen: simulate the room"],[5167,"Every EasyWebinar webinar generates seven links, and the **Share** button on the webinar's header shows them together in one dialog. One is the public registration link you promote; others let a known contact register in one click, let attendees join, let a co-presenter or moderator into the room, and send people to the replay. The dialog also holds the **Registration Widget** embed code, a **Share on social media** section, and a **Shorten URL's** toggle for shorter versions of every link."],[1486,"Every EasyWebinar webinar has an **Analytics** tab that shows how many people reached each stage of that webinar and where the rest dropped away. It has three views: **Overview** for the funnel, engagement and offer numbers, **People** for the individuals behind those numbers, and **Revenue** for what the webinar earned. A date range at the top limits everything on the page to the period you choose."],[5476,"Every EasyWebinar webinar opens on its **Overview** tab. From this one screen you can see how the webinar is doing, check and change when it runs, act on a single session, switch between free and paid registration, add the people who present or moderate, and get to the share links and the room. This page walks through each panel in the order you'll usually need it. When you're done, you'll know where every webinar-level control on the Overview lives and what each number means."],[754,"Every limit, allowance and default setting in EasyWebinar in one place, with its unit and where it applies."],[593,"Every page shows who it applies to, its status and the date it was last checked against the product. Each heading has a permanent link you can copy and share."],[812,"Every plan includes live webinars with browser join. Automation, EasyCRM, checkout and EasyCast start at Growth. AI Moderator answers attendee questions from Pro onward."],[2286,"Every poll on a webinar sits in one list on the CTAs tab. Each one can be switched on or off from that list without being deleted, so a poll can wait in reserve until the point in the session where it fits."],[5214,"Every public link includes your subdomain, ending in `.easywebinar.live`, including the links in your emails. The **C-Name** add-on lets links use your own domain instead. Changing your subdomain changes your existing links, so anything already shared will break; set it before you promote."],[4456,"Every result that matters to the business, from offer clicks to booked calls, depends on people actually watching. That makes reminders matter most to teams that sell or book calls at the end of a session. It matters even more on automated webinars, where sessions run without anyone checking the emails."],[1509,"Every stage up to the demo button happens on the webinar platform: the page visit, the sign-up, the session, the recording and the click. A platform that runs all of those can count every stage for the same webinar, so nobody has to merge lists by hand."],[1236,"Every tile reads zero here because this sample webinar hasn't run. After your session, Replay Watched and Missed are the two to compare once the no-show emails have gone."],[3198,"Every video you add, and every recording of a past webinar, lands in the **Library**. Recordings appear there automatically when **Auto Recording** is on in the live room. See The Library."],[4205,"Every video you add, by either route, appears on the Library's **Videos** tab with a badge in its corner: **EasyWebinar** for a hosted file, or the platform's logo for an imported link. Recordings of live sessions appear on the **Recordings** tab."],[4863,"Every webinar has a registration page hosted by EasyWebinar, and a **Registration Page Link** that sends people to it. The Registration Widget is the other route: instead of sending visitors to EasyWebinar, you bring the form to them, on a page you already control."],[5004,"Every webinar has five pages that its audience moves through: **Registration Page**, **Thank you Page**, **Waiting Area**, **Webinar Page** and **Replay Page**. All five open in the same builder, and all five already know when your webinar runs."],[4303,"Every webinar's **Notifications** tab has three channels: **Emails**, **SMS** and **Whatsapp**. SMS and WhatsApp are in Beta. The **Emails** channel groups everything your webinar sends into five kinds of email:"],[703,"Everyone on the list gets the same follow-up, whether they watched to the end or never turned up. Interested people wait in a spreadsheet while the moment passes. Sales has no way to tell a casual sign-up from someone who clicked the offer."],[87,"Everyone works from one login. Nobody can tell who changed a webinar or a setting, and only one person can host the live room at a time. Anyone holding that password can also reach billing and every account setting, whether their job needs it or not."],[566,"Everything EasyCRM includes: the leads, deals and marketing tools these sending settings serve."],[807,"Everything EasyCRM sends draws on this monthly allowance, and its **Wallet** screen shows what's left. The allowance resets on your **signup date**, not the first of the month. Broadcasts and workflows draw on the same allowance, and each channel is counted separately."],[3708,"Everything you use while presenting sits on the right-hand rail:"],[5145,"Expired links"],[1053,"Few messages, each with its own job"],[2309,"Fill in the **Response Options**. Click **Add another option** for each extra answer, and click the bin beside any option to remove it."],[1988,"Fill in the rest of the offer: **Offer Style** (**Text Offer** or **Image Offer**), **Offer Price** (or switch on **Free**), the **Headline** and **Sub Headline**, and the **Button** text and URL."],[1750,"Fill the chat on a simulive or evergreen webinar with a conversation generated by AI from a cast of simulated attendees, or scripted by you in a timed CSV."],[1435,"Filter **Behavior** for high watch time and offer clicks. Those are people who were interested and haven't bought yet."],[1397,"Filter **People** by **Source & UTM** to see which campaign each registrant came from."],[1428,"Filter by **Behavior** for no-shows, add a **Webinar** filter for a single event, then click **Export**."],[1430,"Filter by **Source & UTM**. You need **UTM Params** turned on in your registration form first."],[5022,"Filter by category: **All Templates**, **Agency**, **Coach**, **Education**, **Health & Wellness**, **Lead Magnet** or **Marketing**. **My Templates** holds templates you've saved yourself."],[2992,"Filter by category: **All Templates**, **Agency**, **Coach**, **Education**, **Health & Wellness**, **Lead Magnet**, **Marketing**, or **My Templates** for ones you have saved."],[1392,"Filter first, then export. Exporting everything and cutting it down in a spreadsheet repeats work the filters already do, and **Export** respects whatever filters are applied."],[446,"Find out who controls the domain's DNS, and agree a time to make the changes."],[1292,"Find people by what they did: the filters to use when you want to write to one group by hand."],[4329,"Find the **Registration Confirmation** group at the top of the list."],[2788,"Find the webinar to copy. The type filters (**All**, **Live**, **Simulive**, **Evergreen**, **Archived**) and search help with a long list."],[573,"Find what you need by role"],[2547,"Find your offers"],[2238,"Find your polls"],[4403,"Find your reminders"],[659,"Find your tool under **Available integrations** and click **Connect**."],[3789,"Find, add and manage the videos, webinar recordings, images and documents your webinars use, see which files count towards your storage, and put a library video to work in a simulive or evergreen webinar."],[255,"First choose how you want to position the offer:"],[824,"Fix it"],[878,"Follow up"],[1441,"Follow up after a course webinar: how a course creator acts on the people who clicked but didn't enrol."],[2412,"Follow-up"],[1943,"Follow-up and CRM tags"],[1315,"Follow-up emails"],[1461,"Follow-up emails"],[2559,"Follow-up emails"],[3959,"Follow-up emails"],[980,"Follow-up emails send after the webinar to the audience you choose: everyone who registered, only those who attended, or only the no-shows. No-shows are usually the biggest group, and the replay link is what they want."],[1070,"Follow-up mistakes that are easy to make today"],[1065,"Follow-up templates for people who clicked or left early"],[1270,"Follow-ups are set per webinar, so a new webinar needs its own set or a clone of an earlier one. The replay link is public while the replay page is on, so anyone you forward it to can watch. EasyWebinar also doesn't host or deliver your course: the offer button and any redirect send people to your own checkout or sales page. SMS (Beta) and WhatsApp (Beta) messages come from an EasyWebinar number, so replies don't reach your phone."],[1223,"Follow-ups belong to one webinar, so your next session needs its own set. Cloning the webinar can bring its email notifications with it, as well as its polls and offers. After cloning, update the dates, the replay link and the deadline in every email."],[4413,"Follow-ups for people the reminders didn't reach"],[519,"For a coach, the reply is often the point of the email, because a reply can start a client conversation. Set **Reply & forwarding settings** with the same care as the identity, and use an address you check daily. A single business address often suits this kind of low-volume sending."],[5205,"For a moderator, to handle chat and questions. Like the co-presenter link, it works without an account. It's also a handy way to check your own webinar from the inside: on a recorded webinar with an embedded third-party chat, joining with the **Moderator Join Link** lets you look at the side panel."],[2027,"For a paid workshop, the registration-page countdown shows how long is left to register before the session starts. Inside the workshop, a countdown on an offer can mark a follow-on programme available to attendees only."],[5204,"For a presenter, so they can join the room. They don't need an EasyWebinar account to use it. When a co-host or moderator joins a live session, they land backstage, not on stage, and your audience doesn't see or hear them until you move them to the stage."],[1499,"For a quick read without opening the tab, the webinar's **Overview** tab shows four live stats (**Registrants**, **Live Attended**, **Total Attended** and **Revenue**) that update as the webinar runs. See The Overview tab."],[1876,"For an automated webinar with simulated chat, pair **Everyone** chat and Chat Simulation with **Private Q&A**, so real questions reach your team in a queue."],[3867,"For an imported video you also enter its length, because EasyWebinar needs the duration to schedule sessions. See Video hosting for both routes step by step."],[228,"For example: a 45-minute live masterclass for experienced freelance designers who want recurring revenue without hiring, covering why hourly billing caps growth, how to turn a repeatable service into a fixed-scope offer, and how to price it. Warm and practical, no hype. End with an offer for a six-week group programme with templates and weekly calls, plus its price."],[3415,"For just-in-time sessions, yes. Daily and weekly sessions run in the webinar's timezone."],[1553,"For paid webinars, the **Revenue** view is where every registration payment and its status appear. See Paid webinars."],[5201,"For people watching the recording afterwards. It's the same link as the **Replay Page Link** on the webinar's **Replay** tab, where you also turn the replay page on with **Enable replay page**."],[5200,"For registered attendees, to enter the live session. Registrants also receive a join link in the **Registration Confirmation** email, which is sent the moment someone registers. That's why it's the one email you shouldn't turn off."],[4733,"For teams that run webinars to generate leads or sell, the registration form is where first-party data starts. It matters most to whoever follows up, in the first days after a session. That's when a role, a phone number or a campaign tag decides who hears from you first."],[3364,"For the scheduled-broadcast version, see Create a simulive webinar."],[4749,"Form changes reach visitors only once the page is published. **Save** keeps a draft; **Publish** makes it public."],[1908,"Four columns, `HH:MM:SS,Name,Role,Message`, saved as UTF-8 CSV. **Download sample CSV** gives you the exact layout."],[3435,"From registration to follow-up"],[4827,"From the Content tab"],[4828,"From the Share dialog"],[1526,"Further down the **Overview**:"],[380,"Further reading"],[1106,"Further reading"],[251,"gathering background"],[249,"gauging interest in your offer"],[2659,"Generated offers appear on the CTAs tab and are edited like any other. Read the copy before you publish, particularly anything about price and what's included."],[276,"Generated pages open in the same drag-and-drop builder as any other, on the webinar's *