ild the offers you sell during the webinar, with an optional countdown."],[3056,"Offers and the countdown timer: put a call to action in front of the room while you present."],[748,"Offers and the countdown timer: the offers behind the **Clicked offer** event."],[2054,"Offers carry over to the replay when the replay page uses **Webinar Replica**. Use **Preview** on the replay page to check it looks the way you want."],[5280,"Offers inside a paid webinar"],[2612,"Offers matter most to teams whose webinars have to pay for themselves, such as course creators, coaches, training companies and product teams. They matter most in launch weeks and on automated webinars, where the card does the selling while nobody is presenting."],[2556,"Offers on the replay"],[2059,"Offers: build the offer card that carries the countdown."],[4092,"Offers: the offers that carry onto a Webinar Replica replay."],[2385,"Offers: the other kind of CTA, built in the same list as your polls."],[551,"On **Configurations**, under **Email Integration** and **Email provider**. **Sending health** sits beside **EasyCRM Mail** on the service list. Look there before your first send, then watch your open rate on the **Broadcasts** screen once mail has gone out."],[2167,"On **Engagement** → **Chat**, choose **Third party**."],[954,"On **My Webinars**, click **⋮** on the webinar's card and choose **Clone Webinar**."],[1670,"On **My Webinars**, click **Create a Webinar**, then **Create Manually**."],[4609,"On **My Webinars**, click **Create a Webinar**, then **Create Manually**."],[2963,"On **Step 2 of 4: Schedule**:"],[2981,"On **Step 3 of 4: Pricing**, choose one:"],[2991,"On **Step 4 of 4: Registration Template**:"],[2487,"On a **simulive** webinar, chat and Q&A work normally. Everyone in a session sees the same moment of the video, and you and your moderators answer in real time while the recording plays."],[2163,"On a busy webinar, one presenter can't watch the chat and present at the same time. The webinar's **Share** dialog includes a **Moderator Join Link for Live room**, which lets a moderator join to handle chat and questions. Treat it as private: anyone holding it can join the room in that role."],[2486,"On a large webinar, a moderator can work the queue while the presenter keeps presenting. Send them the **Moderator Join Link for Live room** from the webinar's **Share** dialog; it is the link for someone handling chat and questions. Keep it private, because anyone holding it can join in that role."],[2016,"On a live webinar you choose the moment to show the offer from the **Offers** panel in the room. Before you go live, **Go Live** reminds you to have offers and polls ready."],[5532,"On a live webinar, **Enter Room** takes you into the webinar room."],[2330,"On a live webinar, polls don't appear on their own: you launch each one manually. When you click **Go Live**, the confirmation reminds you that offers and polls should be ready, so check your poll list in the green room first."],[4043,"On a live webinar, the room header shows **Auto Recording Enabled** when recording is on, and recorded sessions land in **Library → Recordings**. Recording can be changed in the room under **Settings → Recording Settings**. See Run a live webinar and The Library."],[1607,"On a new evergreen webinar"],[4547,"On a new evergreen webinar"],[2053,"On a new live webinar, yes: the registration page builder opens with a countdown to the session. On other types, check the page in the builder. You can restyle the block, hide it on mobile with **Desktop Only**, or remove it."],[5558,"On a paid webinar, **Registrants** counts everyone who has registered and paid, and **Revenue** is the total taken. Every transaction is listed under **Analytics → Revenue → Paid Webinar**."],[4347,"On a paid webinar, the attendee is registered once payment goes through and is then sent to your thank-you page. Purchases of an offer inside the webinar have their own email, **Paid Offer — Transaction Success**, the receipt-style confirmation for anyone who bought. See Paid webinars."],[5026,"On a paid webinar, the template you pick includes the price automatically."],[1816,"On a recorded webinar with an empty chat, the first impression is a room nobody else came to. Attendees already suspect they may be watching a recording, and a silent panel confirms it. Many leave before the content has had a chance to work."],[948,"On a recorded webinar, attendees arrive at different times, so there's no shared conversation, and an empty chat panel makes the room look abandoned. **Chat Simulation** (Beta) fills it, on simulive and evergreen webinars:"],[1878,"On a simulive webinar, everyone in a session watches the same moment, so real chat works and you can answer live while the recording plays. Chat Simulation is available on simulive webinars as well as evergreen ones."],[2488,"On an **evergreen** webinar, Q&A is set up the same way on the Engagement tab. There is also a separate built-in contact form, the **EW Contact Box**, which sends submitted questions to an email address you choose. On a recorded webinar, attendees find it under **Contact** in the room, on its **Question** tab. It is a different thing from the Q&A queue: questions arrive by email rather than in the room's **Question** panel."],[1905,"On an automated webinar, attendees arrive at different times, so a genuine shared chat isn't possible. An empty panel makes the room look deserted."],[3378,"On an automated webinar, people arrive at different times, so a shared live conversation isn't possible. Turn on **Chat Simulation** on the **Engagement** tab to fill the chat with an AI-generated or CSV-scripted conversation. See Chat simulation."],[5511,"On an evergreen webinar with just-in-time switched on, the timezone line reads **Attendee's local timezone**. That's because a just-in-time session starts shortly after each person registers, in their own local time."],[2165,"On an evergreen webinar, a real shared chat