ebinars matter"],[3652,"Why is Continue to Green Room greyed out?"],[1477,"Why is everything showing zero?"],[4704,"Why is my Source & UTM filter empty?"],[1335,"Why is the Phone column empty?"],[369,"Why isn't my CRM email sending?"],[3825,"Why isn't my live session in Recordings?"],[4983,"Why isn't my registration link working?"],[823,"Why it happens"],[1600,"Why just-in-time matters"],[2068,"Why live chat matters"],[2541,"Why offers matter"],[4540,"Why On Demand matters"],[5260,"Why paid webinars matter"],[2232,"Why polls matter"],[2396,"Why Q&A matters"],[4820,"Why registration embeds matter"],[4396,"Why reminders matter"],[3944,"Why replay pages matter"],[3630,"Why running the room well matters"],[2899,"Why scheduling a live webinar matters"],[5122,"Why sharing links matter"],[3074,"Why simulive matters"],[13,"Why team members matter"],[4253,"Why the confirmation email matters"],[3478,"Why the green room matters"],[3802,"Why the Library matters"],[821,"Why the live room can't open your camera or microphone, and how to get into the green room."],[5443,"Why the Overview tab matters"],[1299,"Why the People view matters"],[4948,"Why the registration page builder matters"],[4100,"Why video hosting matters"],[1446,"Why webinar analytics matters"],[326,"Why webinar CRM email sending matters"],[2577,"Why won't my offer save?"],[1783,"Why would I simulate chat?"],[4830,"Widget or link: which to use"],[831,"Will attendees see me while I fix my camera?"],[4992,"Will EasyWebinar translate my page?"],[635,"Will it sync people who registered but didn't attend?"],[894,"Will it work with my email tool?"],[5160,"Will my co-presenter appear on screen as soon as they join?"],[3978,"Will my offers and polls show on the replay?"],[2581,"Will my offers show on the replay?"],[1958,"Will my offers, and their countdowns, show on the replay?"],[2265,"Will my polls appear on the replay?"],[1791,"Will the AI chat be the same in every session?"],[1874,"With **Easywebinar Chat** selected, a recorded webinar's Chat screen offers **Simulated Chat**, which plays back a pre-written chat during the webinar, and **Simulated Attendees**, which shows a simulated attendee list in the room. The script, attendee count and names are set on the Chat Simulation tab. Choosing **Third party** replaces the built-in chat, so simulation stops applying."],[4147,"With **Import from URL**, the answer is somewhere else. You give EasyWebinar the platform, a link and the video's length, and the webinar plays the video from that platform. Nothing is stored on EasyWebinar, so no storage is used, but the webinar now depends on the video staying where it is."],[4146,"With **Local import**, the answer is EasyWebinar. You upload the file, EasyWebinar stores and serves it in the same way a dedicated video host would, and nothing else is needed to play it in a webinar. The upload uses part of your storage allowance, shown at the top of the Library."],[2018,"With **Webinar Replica**, the replay page shows the same video, offers, polls and chat replay as the session, so your offers keep selling after the event. The replay itself can also have a deadline: **Expire after days** closes it a set number of days after the session, and **Specific date** closes it at a time you choose. A replay deadline and an offer deadline are separate settings; keep them consistent so attendees aren't told two different end times."],[868,"With AI"],[1978,"With no countdown, an offer's end point is easy to miss or forget. People who meant to buy are left unsure whether it is still open. Many wait, and in webinar selling, waiting often means not buying. A registration page with no visible start time gives visitors little reason to sign up today."],[4624,"With On Demand off, registrants still have just-in-time or recurring sessions if you've enabled them."],[4732,"With only name and email, you know how many people registered but little else. You can't text anyone, and you can't tell which ad, email or post sent them. The registration count goes up, and the reason why is lost."],[1663,"With only set daily or weekly times, someone who arrives just after a session starts must wait for the next slot. That slot can be hours or a day away. The gap between interest and watching is where people disappear. Many who close the tab meaning to return never do."],[5376,"With the replay page set to **Webinar Replica**, the recording shows the same video, offers, polls and chat replay as the session. Replay availability is set on the **Replay** tab, and **After the replay ends** under Redirects can send viewers to your next offer."],[1354,"Without a behaviour-level list, every registrant gets the same follow-up. The person who watched to the end and clicked your offer gets the same email as someone who never turned up. The people closest to buying are treated like everyone else."],[5013,"Without a registration page, people have nowhere to sign up. Your posts and emails create interest, but that interest never becomes a name on your list. You also lose the first number in your funnel: how many people saw the invitation and said yes."],[4009,"Without a replay page, the session is over for everyone who wasn't there. No-shows get a follow-up with nothing to watch. An offer made live never reaches a second audience. EasyWebinar's guidance is to leave live recording on because the replay is usually watched by more people than the live session."],[3007,"Without a scheduled live session, your audience has no fixed moment to turn up. Promotion has no date to point at, so interest fades before anyone joins. You also lose the chance to answer questions while people are still deciding."],[444,"Without a setup screen, this job happens directly in DNS. These steps show the general method, and they're useful for briefing whoever holds your DNS."],[3888,"Without a shared library, each recorded webinar needs its video added again. Recordings of live sessions sit apart from the webinars that could reuse them. It also gets harder to see which videos depend on an outside platform."],[5550,"Without a single summary screen, the basics of a webinar get scattered. The schedule lives in one place, pricing in another and the presenter list somewhere else. It becomes easy to promote the wrong date. A co-presenter may only get their link after messaging you to ask for it."],[3736,"Without a staging area, presenters test their microphones in front of the audience, and a co-host's first words are an apology about echo. Without a confirmation step, a webinar can start before the offers exist. Without automatic recording, the replay you planned to send to no-shows may not exist at all."],[3531,"Without a staging area, the first minutes of a webinar become the rehearsal. Attendees who arrived on time watch presenters ask whether they can be heard. The recording behind your replay page then opens with the same fumbling."],[4155,"Without a video in place, a simulive or evergreen webinar has nothing to play. Registrants turn up at their session and there is no class to watch. Every webinar you meant to run on its own waits on a file."],[915,"Without a webinar in the middle, people go straight from an email or an ad to a sales page. The page has to answer every doubt on its own, with no chance to teach or take questions. Visitors who aren't ready yet tend to leave."],[4874,"Without an embed, every visitor on your own site has to follow a link to the EasyWebinar page to register. Each extra click is a chance for someone to get distracted and leave. The page that persuaded them, such as the article they were reading, is left behind."],[3370,"Without an evergreen schedule, a recording reaches people only on the dates it is shown. Anyone who finds the page between showings has to wait, and many lose interest before the next one comes round."],[2611,"Without an offer card, the call to action is only what the presenter says. People who arrive late miss it, and anyone watching a recording hears it once and moves on. Interest goes unrecorded, so you can't tell who came close to buying."],[2132,"Without chat, attendees have no way to speak during the session, and the presenter has no way to tell whether the message is landing. Questions go unasked while the moment passes. For a selling webinar, that is where doubts that could have been answered in a sentence turn into \"not now\"."],[2826,"Without cloning, a new format means building the second version by hand. You recreate the registration page, rewrite the emails, re-enter polls and offers and reconnect integrations. Each step is a chance to introduce a difference you didn't intend."],[1122,"Without follow-ups, the webinar ends and so does the conversation. Attendees who meant to decide later get no nudge. Registrants who couldn't make it never learn that a replay exists, even though they asked to hear from you."],[205,"Without it, the setup work is spread across several blank pages: a script document, a page builder, five or six emails and an offer. That's often where webinars stall, especially a first one. Pieces written on different days also tend not to match each other."],[4602,"Without On Demand, every registrant has to wait for a session, even if only for a few minutes. Some content is meant to be watched the moment people find it. For that content, any wait is a chance for them to leave and not return."],[5333,"Without paid registration, the registration page signs up anyone for nothing. A workshop worth paying for becomes a free session. Its value then has to be won back later, through an offer that only some attendees buy."],[1505,"Without per-stage numbers, a disappointing webinar is just disappointing. You can't tell whether few people saw the page, the page didn't convert, the reminders failed or the offer fell flat. So you end up changing everything at once. It's easy to rewrite a talk that was fine, when the real problem was that people never turned up."],[2453,"Without Q&A, attendees have no dedicated place to ask, so many keep their questions to themselves. Those who do ask get no sign that anyone saw the question. You close the session without knowing what the room still wanted to know, and on a selling webinar an unanswered objection often decides the sale."],[4455,"Without reminders, attendance depends on people remembering a session they booked days or weeks ago. Analytics shows the cost as a large **Missed** count: people who registered and never came. EasyWebinar reads a low registered-to-attended rate as a notification problem, not a content one."],[5186,"Without role links, you have to give a guest speaker access to your account to bring them into the room. Without a one-click link, every contact you invite from your own list retypes details you already hold. Some of them won't bother, and those registrations are lost."],[3186,"Without simulive, a repeated presentation means presenting live each time, at whatever hour suits the audience. A fully on-demand recording avoids that. But viewers then arrive at different points, so there is no shared conversation to join."],[4550,"Wording the button"],[841,"Work through these in order and check the device preview after each one."],[462,"Work through these steps in order, and do them before you build anything else in the CRM:"],[343,"Worked example: sizing the garden centre's first month"],[1087,"Worked example: sizing your follow-up lists"],[151,"Write a prompt that works"],[1765,"Write a script that reads like a real room"],[2240,"Write polls people will answer"],[1440,"Write polls people will answer: the **Polls** column only tells you something if people answer them."],[2549,"Write the card"],[4472,"Write the subject and content."],[1056,"Write them in this order if you're sending today"],[1848,"Write your script in the four columns and save the file as **CSV (UTF-8)**."],[557,"Yahoo's sender best practices: the matching rules for all senders and bulk senders, including how Yahoo calculates 